a much more full focused discussion directed

121
00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.910
towards, mostly towards those who are

122
00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:30.600
either already eating a plant-based diet,

123
00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.530
keen on adopting a more plant-centric diet,

124
00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:37.010
or looking to improve upon their plant-based diet

125
00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:40.460
with the goal of essentially setting yourself up

126
00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.293
for success.

127
00:05:41.293 --> 00:05:43.620
And I think the first thing that I want to get into

128
00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.000
or where we can start, would be to begin

129
00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.690
with common blind spots.

130
00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:51.190
So let's say, okay, Simon,

131
00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:52.480
I've been eating a plant-based diet

132
00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.670
for six months, or a year.

133
00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.210
How do I know I'm doing it right?

134
00:05:56.210 --> 00:06:00.850
What are some of the common things that trip people up

135
00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:03.417
or where they go astray, before they have kind of

136
00:06:03.417 --> 00:06:07.973
the full encyclopedic knowledge of how to do this properly?

137
00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.960
There's probably two or three main things

138
00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.536
that I've identified anyway,

139
00:06:14.536 --> 00:06:18.120
in working with many people are going through this,

140
00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.670
and also through my own experience

141
00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.620
and talking to people like you.

142
00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:26.080
I think the first is understanding when you are minimizing

143
00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:30.040
or removing these animal foods that we have grown accustomed

144
00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.510
to eating all the time.

145
00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:32.920
What do you replace them with?

146
00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:35.230
Because there's a lot of different options.

147
00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:39.400
Everything from black beans and lentils

148
00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.633
to very processed vegan foods.

149
00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:48.110
The second would be understanding the difference

150
00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:50.290
between an animal-based diet and a plant-based diet

151
00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:53.010
in terms of calorie density.

152
00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:57.940
So animal foods are typically much more calorie-dense,

153
00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.473
and therefore, if you're wanting to eat

154
00:07:01.473 --> 00:07:03.930
a similar number of calories,

155
00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.390
your plate needs to look fuller

156
00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.437
when it's plant-based foods.

157
00:07:07.437 --> 00:07:09.637
I mean, that's a pretty common thing that you hear like,

158
00:07:09.637 --> 00:07:12.410
"Oh, I tried it, but I was starving all the time."

159
00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:16.020
Yes, and that is something that I personally experienced.

160
00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.190
So as I was making these changes,

161
00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.050
I was not fully cognizant of

162
00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.400
the differences in calorie density.

163
00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.710
And I was experiencing in the very beginning

164
00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.960
of my transition, a little drop in energy.

165
00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.650
And I was doubting whether

166
00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:34.370
the plant-based foods were working for me.

167
00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.630
And really it was just

168
00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:39.070
that I was not consuming enough overall calories.

169
00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:43.180
So understanding what to replace animal foods with,

170
00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:46.700
calorie density, and then the third I'd say, is having

171
00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:51.180
a general awareness of specific nutrients of focus.

172
00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.340
So all diets, whether it's an omnivorous diet

173
00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.250
or a plant-based diet, need to be appropriately planned,

174
00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.810
or they can fall short.

175
00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:03.340
And, if we look around at our current sort

176
00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:06.450
of state of health, the omnivorous diet's

177
00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:07.830
not really serving us that well,

178
00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.760
it has a number of holes and gaps.

179
00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:13.860
And while a plant-based diet can really

180
00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.287
improve your overall disease risk profile.

181
00:08:16.287 --> 00:08:19.080
And we spoke a lot about that in terms of

182
00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.960
shifting these biomarkers in a favorable direction,

183
00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.650
your cholesterol, your blood glucose control,

184
00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.820
inflammation, blood pressure,

185
00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.680
and lower your risk of these chronic diseases

186
00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.920
that are plaguing our society.

187
00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:37.710
At the same time, there are a few nutrients

188
00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.410
that you need to be aware of,

189
00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:43.500
so that are getting them in the required amounts,

190
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.920
to not just prevent your risk of

191
00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.030
these chronic diseases longterm,

192
00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:49.740
but to really optimize yourself

193
00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:52.770
and feel at your best in your day-to-day.

194
00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.850
So the obvious next question being,

195
00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.210
what are those nutrients?

196
00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.043
Yeah.

197
00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.370
So I call these nutrients of focus, and I think

198
00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:05.490
that's a positive spin on nutrients of concern.

199
00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.370
And I just, I want people,

200
00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.060
I wanna draw people's attention to them.

201
00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.870
In the book I write about eight of these,

202
00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.770
and some of are quite easy to get

203
00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:19.920
through your diet and/or fortified foods,

204
00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:24.230
and then others are best accessed through a supplement.

205
00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:28.430
So as a list, these are vitamin B12,

206
00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:33.430
vitamin D, omega-3 fatty acids, iodine,

207
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.660
iron, calcium, zinc, and selenium.

208
00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:39.660
Right.

209
00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:44.660
So given that, a skeptic would say, well,

210
00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:47.590
if I have to pay extra close attention to these things,

211
00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:51.660
or I have to go outside of my food

212
00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:53.830
that I'm consuming and supplement,

213
00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:57.833
then this must be a deficient diet by definition.

214
00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.850
I think we need to zoom out a little bit

215
00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:07.000
and understand that nutritional gaps are nothing new.

216
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.940
And it's the very reason that folate

217
00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.700
and iodine have been used throughout the food system,

218
00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:16.550
fortifying foods to prevent iodine deficiency

219
00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.650
and folate deficiency in the general public.

220
00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:24.240
So this idea of fortificational supplements is nothing new

221
00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:27.310
and lots of those nutrients I just reeled off,

222
00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.900
like zinc, selenium, iron, calcium,

223
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.597
you can easily access them through your diet

224
00:10:31.597 --> 00:10:33.550
and you don't need to supplement those.

225
00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:36.540
It's just a matter of understanding what foods do you want

226
00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.190
to be incorporating in your diet regularly?

227
00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:42.330
And for example, if you're choosing a plant-based milk

228
00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.130
to swap out dairy, which is rich in calcium,

229
00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:46.833
what should you be looking for?

230
00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.210
And I would add to that,

231
00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:53.400
that I understand there are certain people

232
00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.840
that are very anti-supplements and therefore,

233
00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:00.511
that must make this the incorrect diet

234
00:11:00.511 --> 00:11:03.200
for optimal health and wellbeing.

235
00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:08.200
But not everything that is unnatural is bad for us.

236
00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:15.040
And there have been many parts of our life,

237
00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:18.240
be it modern housing or climate control,

238
00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.930
that have improved our wellbeing,

239
00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:23.770
so I think just presuming that everything

240
00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:28.380
that is natural is best is somewhat of a fallacy.

241
00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:31.160
And what we should be worried most

242
00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:33.060
about is heart health outcomes.

243
00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:35.970
So I have nothing against a diet

244
00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:38.200
that includes some supplementation.

245
00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.710
It means the best outcomes for,

246
00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.830
be it for myself or anyone that I'm working with.

247
00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.000
And that is what the data suggests.

248
00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.950
If you wanna move down this path of very plant-rich,

249
00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:53.630
plant-predominant diets, or even plant-exclusive

250
00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:58.030
to lower your risk of chronic disease,

251
00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:00.070
then taking some of these supplements is going

252
00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.640
to allow you to do that in a more optimal manner.

253
00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:03.490
Right.

254
00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:07.070
Certainly things like vitamin D deficiencies

255
00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:10.280
are not endemic to the plant-based community.

256
00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:12.350
I mean, this is something that omnivores,

257
00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:15.820
that a lot of people, perhaps even the majority of people

258
00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:19.380
who are not living on the equator experience, right?

259
00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.900
Sure, and you could say the same about vitamin B12.

260
00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.540
There was a study done recently,

261
00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.910
an American population over 3,000 people and 39% of

262
00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:33.000
the omnivores in there had insufficient B12 status.

263
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.580
So you're right, the nutritional deficiencies

264
00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.580
are not just something that plant-predominant

265
00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:42.270
or plant-exclusive eaters experience.

266
00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:43.550
And I think we could all agree

267
00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:45.130
that the supplement industry,

268
00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.700
the billion dollar supplement industry,

269
00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.553
is not propped up by vegans.

270
00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:54.380
So there's a bit to sort of weigh up there,

271
00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:57.240
but the most important thing that I kind of,

272
00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.850
the point that I wanna make here,

273
00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:02.150
is that most of this is very easily covered.

274
00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:04.810
And it's just a matter of taking some time

275
00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:06.290
to get across the information.

276
00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.410
And then you set and forget,

277
00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:11.910
and you focus on the overall quality of your diet,

278
00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.970
and you have a few supplements or fortified foods,

279
00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:16.610
and you can have peace of mind that you're

280
00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:20.250
getting everything that you need in required amounts.

281
00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.920
One question that I've always had,

282
00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.330
and I'm not sure I've ever asked it to anybody,

283
00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:27.223
certainly nobody of your experience.

284
00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:31.520
Is there a difference between taking

285
00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:34.270
like a specific B12 supplement,

286
00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:37.510
either a spray or a sublingual, or something like that,

287
00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.180
and a D and a zinc, whatever,

288
00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.110
taking those individually versus getting

289
00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:42.610
a really good multivitamin

290
00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:44.363
that has kind of everything in it?

291
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.150
This is a great question.

292
00:13:48.353 --> 00:13:50.870
And some of this comes down to

293
00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:52.894
the person we're talking about.

294
00:13:52.894 --> 00:13:55.970
I know that some people

295
00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:59.260
who are completely okay with supplements,

296
00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:01.980
will be happy just taking a multivitamin,

297
00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.020
knowing that a lot of those nutrients in there,

298
00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:07.137
they're already getting in the amounts that they require.

299
00:14:07.137 --> 00:14:10.557
Right, you get the bright yellow pee.

300
00:14:10.557 --> 00:14:12.280
Yeah, so a lot of the B vitamins,

301
00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.130
you're already getting a lot of those

302
00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.883
through a very plant-rich diet,

303
00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.700
particularly folate, for example,

304
00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:19.900
you're getting it in abundance.

305
00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:22.293
You don't really need to be supplementing that,

306
00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:26.650
but some people just like to take a multivitamin

307
00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:27.606
and that's okay.

308
00:14:27.606 --> 00:14:30.640
I am an advocate for taking a multivitamin,

309
00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.210
if that's the path you want to go down.

310
00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:34.570
There are some things to think about with the multivitamins

311
00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:38.220
because they're not all formulated for plant-predominant,

312
00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:39.210
plant-rich people.

313
00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:42.748
So there are some things to look at specifically,

314
00:14:42.748 --> 00:14:46.113
and then others prefer to take individual supplements,

315
00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:51.480
which can mean having to buy multiple different supplements.

316
00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:52.660
And it's not as convenient,

317
00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.250
but there are a number of brands now coming out

318
00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:57.210
that are creating multi-nutrients,

319
00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:00.450
specific for the needs of someone who is adopting

320
00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:01.665
a plant-based dietary pattern.

321
00:15:01.665 --> 00:15:05.350
Like Matt Frazier has a multivitamin

322
00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:06.950
that's sort of specific to people

323
00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:08.300
who are eating a plant-based diet.

324
00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.130
That's directed towards the nutrients

325
00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.860
that perhaps you might be lacking.

326
00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.220
Yeah, and I think those are great options

327
00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.560
because they've done the work,

328
00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:19.920
they've realized you don't need all of these other vitamins

329
00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.440
and minerals you're already getting,

330
00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.950
and they've worked out calculated through science,

331
00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:27.133
so data-driven,

332
00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.500
how much of each of these nutrients are focused,

333
00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:33.140
do you actually need, and therefore

334
00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:37.230
you end up with a more personalized supplement.

335
00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:39.767
So with respect to B12,

336
00:15:39.767 --> 00:15:42.710
there's different types of that, there's methylcobalamin

337
00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.090
and then there's cobalamin,

338
00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.347
like which one should you be selecting?

339
00:15:46.347 --> 00:15:49.880
And hydroxycobalamin, and adeno, so cobalamin.

340
00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.443
It all gets very confusing.

341
00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.550
My position is that the most-studied version

342
00:15:55.550 --> 00:16:00.160
is cyanocobalamin and, for preventing deficiency

343
00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.180
and reversing it.

344
00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:03.480
And therefore the dosages that we have,

345
00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.950
the recommended amounts of B12 to take

346
00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:09.800
are largely from studies looking at that type.

347
00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:14.400
So my recommendation is to buy

348
00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.500
a sciatica-balumin B12 supplement,

349
00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:22.090
and you'd be looking at 250 micrograms daily,

350
00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:25.410
or two and a half thousand micrograms once a week.

351
00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.320
Those are your two options.

352
00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:29.600
Now I should add to that.

353
00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:33.490
If you are a smoker or you have kidney disease,

354
00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.430
that's two instances where methylcobalamin

355
00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.073
is certainly better.

356
00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.730
And then I would also add, if your supplement

357
00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.373
contains methylcobalamin,

358
00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.270
I have worked with many people

359
00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:49.940
who have used that form and have completely fine B12 status,

360
00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:52.800
so they all seem to work.

361
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:55.560
My preference being cyanocobalamin is purely

362
00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:59.080
because that's what most of the science has looked at.

363
00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:03.420
Because it's more bio available or it converts better?

364
00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.440
Well, it tends to be used in the studies more

365
00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.603
because it's cheaper,

366
00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:09.300
and more widely available.

367
00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:12.770
But we have seen it in the last, I'd say five or so years,

368
00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:15.420
a lot more brands you using methylcobalamin.

369
00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.120
And I think that's okay.

370
00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:19.540
My recommendation for most of this stuff

371
00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:23.300
is your laboratory tests will really tell the story.

372
00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:25.810
Yeah, and that's a great objective way

373
00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:29.150
of keeping an eye on any of these nutrients,

374
00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.750
and just periodically keeping

375
00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.080
an eye on your overall health.

376
00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:36.100
I think it's a good idea with B12,

377
00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:37.210
it's worth mentioning,

378
00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:39.060
if you're doing a blood test,

379
00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:42.120
the standard blood test that your physician

380
00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.710
would order is serum B12.

381
00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:48.850
And that's a pretty good marker, but it's not perfect.

382
00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:53.850
There are active and inactive B12 molecules in our body.

383
00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:57.530
And the serum B12 test does pick up

384
00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.600
some of the inactive analogs.

385
00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:04.060
And so the general rule of thumb is

386
00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.850
if you get a serum B12 test, and it comes back,

387
00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.530
and you're at the middle or upper part of the range,

388
00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:10.620
then you probably don't need

389
00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.260
to look into things any further.

390
00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:14.280
But if you're more towards the lower end

391
00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.560
of the normal range, then there is another test

392
00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:20.680
called MMA that you can request,

393
00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.790
which is more specific and sensitive to active B12.

394
00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:28.080
So, most people won't need to worry about that,

395
00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.270
but that's one just to be mindful of,

396
00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:33.250
if your B12 is little low,

397
00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.820
and perhaps you are subjectively feeling

398
00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:38.270
like you don't have a lot of energy.

399
00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:41.100
And when we're talking about vitamin D,

400
00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.350
is there a difference between D and D3,

401
00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:45.450
or are those terms conflated?

402
00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:46.700
Those are the same thing.

403
00:18:48.037 --> 00:18:50.860
D3 is the type of vitamin D

404
00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:54.620
that your body will produce following sun exposure.

405
00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:56.040
And it's also found

406
00:18:56.040 --> 00:19:00.450
in animal products, and found in plant lichen,

407
00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:02.380
which is a type of algae.

408
00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:05.360
And then there is D2, which is found in mushrooms,

409
00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:07.403
but D2 or D3

410
00:19:07.403 --> 00:19:11.360
will both increase your vitamin D status.

411
00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:15.130
It's important to add that 80,

412
00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:20.130
90% of your vitamin D status is determined by sun exposure.

413
00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:25.400
So very little contribution from the foods

414
00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:30.280
that we eat, and that status,

415
00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:35.280
it be really affected by how dark your skin is,

416
00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:39.010
that where you live in the world.

417
00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:43.375
If you live at a Northern latitude, you are more at risk

418
00:19:43.375 --> 00:19:46.493
of developing vitamin D deficiency.

419
00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:50.040
What is the, what are the symptoms of,

420
00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.780
how does that manifest?

421
00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.270
It could be an impaired immune system

422
00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:56.053
is one of the main ones.

423
00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:02.520
And so whether someone needs to supplement vitamin D

424
00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:06.010
is debated around the world heavily.

425
00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.750
And even the reference ranges

426
00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.113
are heavily debated country-to-country.

427
00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:16.030
My general sort of advice here is

428
00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:20.400
unless you're getting daily sun exposure,

429
00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:24.210
and that sun exposure, the rule of thumb is

430
00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:27.160
about half of the time it would take

431
00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:30.980
for you to burn is the amount of time in the sun

432
00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:33.830
it would take to produce adequate amount of vitamin D.

433
00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:38.160
Yeah, I mean, translation is the sun exposure required

434
00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:40.900
to produce inadequate amount of vitamin D is much more

435
00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:42.200
than I think people think.

436
00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:48.150
And as I said, if you have darker skin pigmentation,

437
00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:51.980
you need to be in the sun for longer to produce

438
00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.490
the same amount of vitamin D as someone with fairer skin.

439
00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.240
And this is why we see people with darker skin

440
00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:02.110
more at risk of vitamin D deficiency.

441
00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:07.110
So you can do a hydroxy vitamin D test

442
00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:13.770
and determine whether you are low

443
00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:15.490
or you're at a healthy level.

444
00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:17.240
That could be your starting point.

445
00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:20.300
And so someone like you here in Los Angeles

446
00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:25.300
and myself in Sydney, sun exposure may be completely fine.

447
00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:26.863
It might be adequate for us.

448
00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:30.320
But then someone living in the United Kingdom

449
00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:33.880
or perhaps, part of Canada, it could be a little different.

450
00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:38.880
And if you are on the low side,

451
00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:42.110
the general rule of thumb for supplementation

452
00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:46.670
is about 1,000 to 2,000 IU.

453
00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:50.630
And there are a few different vitamin D supplements

454
00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.740
out there, as I mentioned.

455
00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.600
So a lot of them are actually not plant-based.

456
00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:57.220
They're derived from wool.

457
00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:58.510
So if you are looking for one.

458
00:21:58.510 --> 00:21:59.343
I didn't know that.

459
00:21:59.343 --> 00:22:01.800
If you're looking for one that is vegan,

460
00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.450
if that's important to you,

461
00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:08.450
then you want to find either vitamin D3 from plant lichen,

462
00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:13.000
and essentially any brand selling vitamin D3

463
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:16.650
that is vegan will call out vegan on the packaging.

464
00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:19.463
Or, the other option is vitamin D2 from mushroom.

465
00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:23.170
Is there a specific brand that you recommend

466
00:22:25.021 --> 00:22:26.180
or you steer clear of that?

467
00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:29.130
I generally do steer a little clear

468
00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:29.963
of recommending brands.

469
00:22:29.963 --> 00:22:32.950
However, I will say, because I'm asked this all the time,

470
00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:37.950
I have put together a PDF, and I'm kind of nearly finished.

471
00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:39.650
It's been a huge project

472
00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:42.920
because trying to find the right supplements

473
00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:47.010
depending on someone's age or whether their lifestyle stage,

474
00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:48.680
for example, prenatal,

475
00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:52.400
and then looking what's available around the entire world.

476
00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:54.677
I can send you that PDF,

477
00:22:54.677 --> 00:22:57.177
and you can perhaps put that on your website.

478
00:22:57.177 --> 00:22:59.140
Yeah, maybe we can link that up in the show notes,

479
00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:00.600
'cause this isn't going up for a while.

480
00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.370
So maybe by then you'll be done with it.

481
00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:04.313
I will be done by then,

482
00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:07.800
but I have been reluctant to kind of associate

483
00:23:07.800 --> 00:23:09.510
with too many brands in the past,

484
00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:12.123
but it is such a regular question I get,

485
00:23:12.123 --> 00:23:13.960
that I kind of thought, well,

486
00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:16.180
I need to go through this process.

487
00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:18.820
So that will definitely be made available.

488
00:23:18.820 --> 00:23:21.370
And I should just add to this

489
00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:25.920
that if someone is overweight or obese,

490
00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:29.380
their requirement for vitamin D is actually higher.

491
00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:34.380
So in that instance, it can require sort of two to 3,000 IU

492
00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.270
to achieve a healthy vitamin D status.

493
00:23:37.270 --> 00:23:40.110
So worth just keeping in mind.

494
00:23:40.110 --> 00:23:41.520
Two questions.

495
00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:45.590
Is there any reason or efficacy behind,

496
00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:48.660
like megadosing any of these, like is there

497
00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:51.710
a minimum effective dose in that you're,

498
00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:53.840
once you meet your requirements, you're good?

499
00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:56.140
Or, is there any added benefit

500
00:23:56.140 --> 00:23:59.460
from taking over that amount is the first question.

501
00:23:59.460 --> 00:24:03.410
And then the second is, if you are deficient,

502
00:24:03.410 --> 00:24:08.410
how long does it to restore your balance?

503
00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:14.760
I assume it's not just one vitamin and then you're good.

504
00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:16.720
Like it's gonna take a while, right?

505
00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:18.910
Yeah, weeks, weeks to months, it can take,

506
00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:20.950
depending on the nutrient that we're talking about,

507
00:24:20.950 --> 00:24:24.403
and how low someone is and what dose you give them.

508
00:24:25.275 --> 00:24:29.580
megadosing, look, I would not be recommending doing that

509
00:24:29.580 --> 00:24:32.470
unless it's under the guidance of your physician

510
00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:35.730
and there's a very compelling reason to be doing that.

511
00:24:35.730 --> 00:24:38.510
You hear all sorts of things and ideas online,

512
00:24:38.510 --> 00:24:41.440
like megadosing vitamin D, for example,

513
00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:43.500
the upper limit of vitamin D is set

514
00:24:43.500 --> 00:24:47.640
at about 3,000 to 4,000 IU in Australia.

515
00:24:47.640 --> 00:24:52.260
And the sort of studies looking at toxicity

516
00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:56.743
have shown that up to 10,000 IU is still safe.

517
00:24:57.840 --> 00:25:01.740
However, I think given that the published upper limit

518
00:25:01.740 --> 00:25:04.013
is I believe 4,000 IU,

519
00:25:04.990 --> 00:25:09.430
I would be hesitant to recommend anyone does that megadosing

520
00:25:09.430 --> 00:25:12.900
without their physician overlooking it.

521
00:25:12.900 --> 00:25:14.420
All right, got it.

522
00:25:14.420 --> 00:25:17.380
You mentioned iodine earlier

523
00:25:17.380 --> 00:25:19.430
in this list of eight nutrients.

524
00:25:19.430 --> 00:25:22.080
So why is that important and what are

525
00:25:22.080 --> 00:25:23.980
the foods that we should be looking at

526
00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:26.873
to make sure that we're meeting our iodine needs?

527
00:25:26.873 --> 00:25:29.460
Yeah, this one's often forgotten.

528
00:25:29.460 --> 00:25:33.130
And so it deserves a bit more air time.

529
00:25:33.130 --> 00:25:37.810
So iodine is integral to our thyroid hormone production,

530
00:25:37.810 --> 00:25:39.543
