2069
01:42:39.855 --> 01:42:41.281
so a millimole--

2070
01:42:41.281 --> 01:42:44.580
One millimole is 62 milligrams.

2071
01:42:44.580 --> 01:42:45.780
Okay, that's a big difference.

2072
01:42:45.780 --> 01:42:47.810
I wanna really clarify that.

2073
01:42:47.810 --> 01:42:52.810
And so you're targeting 300 to 530 milligrams.

2074
01:42:53.770 --> 01:42:54.680
Okay, that's not very much.

2075
01:42:54.680 --> 01:42:57.140
So how much would be in a typical beet?

2076
01:42:57.140 --> 01:43:00.120
So to hit that 530 milligrams,

2077
01:43:00.120 --> 01:43:04.483
I've calculated at three and a half medium size beetroots.

2078
01:43:05.420 --> 01:43:07.050
Beetroot, that's an Australian thing.

2079
01:43:07.050 --> 01:43:08.410
So the, when you say beetroot,

2080
01:43:08.410 --> 01:43:11.110
that means the beet with the greens on top of it.

2081
01:43:11.110 --> 01:43:12.360
Just the beet.
Or just the beet.

2082
01:43:12.360 --> 01:43:13.193
Just the beet.

2083
01:43:13.193 --> 01:43:15.010
And what is the, like, I always put,

2084
01:43:15.010 --> 01:43:17.520
when I'm making a smoothie, I take the greens.

2085
01:43:17.520 --> 01:43:19.820
You go to the grocery store, they rip the greens off,

2086
01:43:19.820 --> 01:43:21.050
and they want to toss 'em away.

2087
01:43:21.050 --> 01:43:23.140
But I love the greens and I put those

2088
01:43:23.140 --> 01:43:25.020
in the smoothie as well or I cook them.

2089
01:43:25.020 --> 01:43:27.500
Yeah, they'll will contain nitrates as well.

2090
01:43:27.500 --> 01:43:28.550
But at a lesser.

2091
01:43:28.550 --> 01:43:31.310
Yeah, the study that I saw that looked

2092
01:43:31.310 --> 01:43:33.900
at nitrate content was just looking at the beet.

2093
01:43:33.900 --> 01:43:37.010
Got it.
Which was, and I calculated,

2094
01:43:37.010 --> 01:43:39.980
you would need three and a half medium-sized beets

2095
01:43:39.980 --> 01:43:41.270
to get to that 530.

2096
01:43:41.270 --> 01:43:42.152
That's a lot.
That's a lot.

2097
01:43:42.152 --> 01:43:43.180
That's a lot.

2098
01:43:43.180 --> 01:43:47.423
And that's probably why the powders have become so popular.

2099
01:43:48.370 --> 01:43:52.040
And so you just need to find one that has,

2100
01:43:52.040 --> 01:43:55.420
is supplying 530 milligrams.

2101
01:43:55.420 --> 01:43:59.610
And I think we should probably also make it clear here

2102
01:43:59.610 --> 01:44:04.300
that with all of these supplements, nitrates included,

2103
01:44:04.300 --> 01:44:06.010
if you are a professional athlete,

2104
01:44:06.010 --> 01:44:08.360
you need to be working with your club dietician.

2105
01:44:08.360 --> 01:44:12.460
They will be considering what brands you can and cannot buy.

2106
01:44:12.460 --> 01:44:14.240
Often, you need to buy brands that have gone

2107
01:44:14.240 --> 01:44:15.930
through specific testing.

2108
01:44:15.930 --> 01:44:18.670
And there has been issues where what's in,

2109
01:44:18.670 --> 01:44:21.400
what the ingredient label says is

2110
01:44:21.400 --> 01:44:24.480
in the product is not actually what's in there.

2111
01:44:24.480 --> 01:44:25.630
So you kind of, if you're going

2112
01:44:25.630 --> 01:44:27.330
to add these things into your regime

2113
01:44:27.330 --> 01:44:28.530
and your professional athletes,

2114
01:44:28.530 --> 01:44:30.823
sit down with the right people.

2115
01:44:32.310 --> 01:44:37.310
Is there any thoughts around usage in terms of cycling?

2116
01:44:38.050 --> 01:44:40.360
Like, is this something that you could do every day?

2117
01:44:40.360 --> 01:44:42.830
And it's just like, if you're training really hard,

2118
01:44:42.830 --> 01:44:45.550
should you use it daily or should you use it

2119
01:44:45.550 --> 01:44:47.950
for a period of time, get off it, go back on it?

2120
01:44:48.960 --> 01:44:53.260
I'm not sure there is enough data to say

2121
01:44:53.260 --> 01:44:55.594
what is the best option there.

2122
01:44:55.594 --> 01:44:58.740
So far, the data is suggesting that it's completely safe

2123
01:44:58.740 --> 01:45:00.930
to take that on a daily basis,

2124
01:45:00.930 --> 01:45:05.630
but whether coming on and off is a more effective strategy

2125
01:45:05.630 --> 01:45:07.800
and leads to greater efficiency longterm,

2126
01:45:07.800 --> 01:45:09.840
I don't think that's been teased out.

2127
01:45:09.840 --> 01:45:11.970
Are there, I want to kind of slide

2128
01:45:11.970 --> 01:45:15.280
into a conversation about supplements

2129
01:45:15.280 --> 01:45:18.640
for athletes more broadly, but on the subject

2130
01:45:18.640 --> 01:45:23.050
of beetroot and nitrates, and nitrites,

2131
01:45:23.050 --> 01:45:24.980
is there a supplement,

2132
01:45:24.980 --> 01:45:28.300
like why not go right directly to the nitrous oxide?

2133
01:45:28.300 --> 01:45:31.360
Like, can you, is there a supplement

2134
01:45:31.360 --> 01:45:34.270
where you could just, in capsule form,

2135
01:45:34.270 --> 01:45:37.273
take nitrous oxide and achieve the effect

2136
01:45:37.273 --> 01:45:41.490
that the beetroot active ingredient is producing?

2137
01:45:41.490 --> 01:45:43.010
I don't think it's that easy.

2138
01:45:43.010 --> 01:45:47.080
From my read, is if you want to actually absorb it

2139
01:45:47.080 --> 01:45:50.600
and increase nitric oxide levels in the body,

2140
01:45:50.600 --> 01:45:52.850
you have to deliver one of the precursors.

2141
01:45:52.850 --> 01:45:55.660
And that is either nitrates or the other one

2142
01:45:55.660 --> 01:46:00.440
that you will see is L Citrulline.

2143
01:46:00.440 --> 01:46:03.170
And L Citrulline is another supplement

2144
01:46:03.170 --> 01:46:06.230
that will boost nitric oxide in the body.

2145
01:46:06.230 --> 01:46:09.200
It does it by raising arginine levels,

2146
01:46:09.200 --> 01:46:11.950
which then a converted by a completely different pathway

2147
01:46:11.950 --> 01:46:13.000
to what we've spoken about.

2148
01:46:13.000 --> 01:46:16.580
It's an endogenous pathway way to nitric oxide.

2149
01:46:16.580 --> 01:46:21.580
So as far as I'm aware, you need to provide a precursor.

2150
01:46:21.720 --> 01:46:25.640
And that has to be in the form of nitrates or L Citrulline.

2151
01:46:25.640 --> 01:46:28.140
My preference of the two is nitrates,

2152
01:46:28.140 --> 01:46:30.070
because there's been more study on them.

2153
01:46:30.070 --> 01:46:30.903
Got it.

2154
01:46:32.320 --> 01:46:34.760
I'm just gonna eat my beets.

2155
01:46:34.760 --> 01:46:35.650
Am I good with that?

2156
01:46:35.650 --> 01:46:36.630
That's what I do.
All right.

2157
01:46:36.630 --> 01:46:37.903
For what it's worth.

2158
01:46:38.780 --> 01:46:40.910
Supplements for athletes.

2159
01:46:40.910 --> 01:46:44.950
At the top of this pyramid, obviously protein powders.

2160
01:46:44.950 --> 01:46:46.210
So let's talk about that.

2161
01:46:46.210 --> 01:46:51.210
Like, do we need to be taking protein powders?

2162
01:46:52.040 --> 01:46:54.560
How much, is this advisable?

2163
01:46:54.560 --> 01:46:55.770
When should we take it?

2164
01:46:55.770 --> 01:47:00.770
And which types of plant protein extracts are optimal?

2165
01:47:01.598 --> 01:47:02.431
And there's a lot in that question.

2166
01:47:02.431 --> 01:47:03.823
It's a lot there.

2167
01:47:04.770 --> 01:47:06.360
It's going to be context-dependent.

2168
01:47:06.360 --> 01:47:08.540
I will say, I think most athletes certainly

2169
01:47:08.540 --> 01:47:11.700
that I work with or spoken to, find a protein powder

2170
01:47:11.700 --> 01:47:16.700
a very convenient way to get 30 grams of protein in.

2171
01:47:17.970 --> 01:47:19.760
And it's also a little less filling

2172
01:47:19.760 --> 01:47:22.270
than always eating legumes.

2173
01:47:22.270 --> 01:47:25.990
So I think it certainly has utility,

2174
01:47:25.990 --> 01:47:29.790
but I will say that you can still build muscle

2175
01:47:29.790 --> 01:47:31.513
and perform very well without it.

2176
01:47:32.450 --> 01:47:33.690
Yeah, I had Robert Cheeke here

2177
01:47:33.690 --> 01:47:35.360
and he was talking about his history

2178
01:47:35.360 --> 01:47:37.850
with this going from, and mine is similar,

2179
01:47:37.850 --> 01:47:41.230
like having a pantry full of all kinds of powders,

2180
01:47:41.230 --> 01:47:42.063
then thinking like,

2181
01:47:42.063 --> 01:47:44.900
is this doing anything and weaning himself off of it,

2182
01:47:44.900 --> 01:47:47.840
and realizing that without any of it,

2183
01:47:47.840 --> 01:47:52.140
he was making gains that he wasn't capable of prior.

2184
01:47:52.140 --> 01:47:55.090
And his point being like, maybe they have use,

2185
01:47:55.090 --> 01:47:57.380
but they shouldn't come at the cost

2186
01:47:57.380 --> 01:48:00.710
of sourcing your nutrients from whole foods.

2187
01:48:00.710 --> 01:48:02.560
And if you're meeting those needs,

2188
01:48:02.560 --> 01:48:04.990
is there any advantage at all to even doing this

2189
01:48:04.990 --> 01:48:07.980
in the first place, the powders?

2190
01:48:07.980 --> 01:48:11.670
So the advantage can be, if you are trying

2191
01:48:11.670 --> 01:48:15.420
to lower your total caloric intake, for example,

2192
01:48:15.420 --> 01:48:17.600
then it's a very concentrated source of protein

2193
01:48:17.600 --> 01:48:19.183
for a small amount of calories.

2194
01:48:20.200 --> 01:48:23.060
So depending on the type of athlete,

2195
01:48:23.060 --> 01:48:25.300
that might be something that they're trying to do,

2196
01:48:25.300 --> 01:48:26.742
and therefore it has good utility.

2197
01:48:26.742 --> 01:48:28.882
That makes sense.

2198
01:48:28.882 --> 01:48:32.500
I'm a minimalist, relative minimalist

2199
01:48:32.500 --> 01:48:34.100
when it comes to supplements,

2200
01:48:34.100 --> 01:48:36.790
but I do have a protein powder, and I usually throw

2201
01:48:36.790 --> 01:48:40.213
a scoop or so into a smoothie that I have every day.

2202
01:48:42.560 --> 01:48:44.550
My recommendation for trying to choose one,

2203
01:48:44.550 --> 01:48:48.610
because there's so many on the market is,

2204
01:48:48.610 --> 01:48:53.610
firstly, 25 to 30 grams of protein in a serve as a minimum.

2205
01:48:54.130 --> 01:48:56.240
Sometimes you see some coming out now

2206
01:48:56.240 --> 01:49:00.573
and they're diluted down to 15, 16 grams.

2207
01:49:01.881 --> 01:49:05.410
You need 25, 30 grams as a minimum

2208
01:49:05.410 --> 01:49:07.840
to maximize muscle protein synthesis,

2209
01:49:07.840 --> 01:49:09.640
if that's your goal.

2210
01:49:09.640 --> 01:49:13.630
Secondly is, I like to look for one

2211
01:49:13.630 --> 01:49:15.707
that has the amino acid profile.

2212
01:49:15.707 --> 01:49:17.210
And this goes back to our trade off

2213
01:49:17.210 --> 01:49:18.800
we were talking about before,

2214
01:49:18.800 --> 01:49:20.090
because if you're an athlete

2215
01:49:20.090 --> 01:49:25.090
and you are looking to boost your performance,

2216
01:49:25.150 --> 01:49:27.150
then leucine is important.

2217
01:49:27.150 --> 01:49:28.730
And you can find one that has two

2218
01:49:28.730 --> 01:49:31.700
to three grams of leucine per serve,

2219
01:49:31.700 --> 01:49:36.030
and know that that's going to be a very anabolic protein.

2220
01:49:36.030 --> 01:49:39.160
So firstly, does it have enough protein per serve?

2221
01:49:39.160 --> 01:49:42.610
Secondly, looking at the leucine content.

2222
01:49:42.610 --> 01:49:45.320
Over and beyond that, I usually tell people

2223
01:49:45.320 --> 01:49:46.920
to find one that they enjoy.

2224
01:49:46.920 --> 01:49:50.490
They like the brand Ethos, it tastes good.

2225
01:49:50.490 --> 01:49:53.190
And they're kind of the two most important things

2226
01:49:53.190 --> 01:49:55.780
I'm looking at from a performance point-of-view.

2227
01:49:55.780 --> 01:49:57.910
There are a lot of different blends and different types,

2228
01:49:57.910 --> 01:50:00.920
you've got potato protein is now starting

2229
01:50:00.920 --> 01:50:04.180
to surface, pumpkin, you've got brown rice,

2230
01:50:04.180 --> 01:50:06.560
you've got pea protein.

2231
01:50:06.560 --> 01:50:09.500
You've got mung bean, fava, there's a whole lot coming out.

2232
01:50:09.500 --> 01:50:12.820
Yeah, we have hemp, Sacha Inchi, chia,

2233
01:50:12.820 --> 01:50:15.070
I'm seeing now, sunflower, all different kinds.

2234
01:50:15.070 --> 01:50:17.410
So yeah, I mean, my obvious question is

2235
01:50:17.410 --> 01:50:20.900
which one of those has the best profile

2236
01:50:20.900 --> 01:50:24.410
for athletic performance, or which one of those

2237
01:50:24.410 --> 01:50:26.893
has a better leucine profile?

2238
01:50:29.400 --> 01:50:34.220
Typically speaking, the pea protein,

2239
01:50:34.220 --> 01:50:37.490
brown rice protein blend is like

2240
01:50:37.490 --> 01:50:39.230
the plant-based whey protein.

2241
01:50:39.230 --> 01:50:40.803
That's the most common that you see.

2242
01:50:40.803 --> 01:50:42.100
It's the most common.

2243
01:50:42.100 --> 01:50:44.090
And it is for a reason in that

2244
01:50:44.090 --> 01:50:45.760
when you put those two together,

2245
01:50:45.760 --> 01:50:48.040
you get a very similar amino acid profile

2246
01:50:48.040 --> 01:50:52.371
to whey protein, so without over complicating things,

2247
01:50:52.371 --> 01:50:56.440
that's a great worthy option for anyone.

2248
01:50:56.440 --> 01:50:59.570
With that said, if you stick to the first two principles

2249
01:50:59.570 --> 01:51:02.420
that I said of 25 to 30 grams,

2250
01:51:02.420 --> 01:51:04.900
two to three grams of leucine,

2251
01:51:04.900 --> 01:51:08.030
then I'm not so concerned really what that blend is.

2252
01:51:08.030 --> 01:51:10.683
It could be a, it could be for four or five of those.

2253
01:51:11.540 --> 01:51:13.980
And I'm more interested at that point

2254
01:51:13.980 --> 01:51:17.290
in what someone likes in terms of palatability.

2255
01:51:17.290 --> 01:51:20.400
And therefore they're going to be happy with,

2256
01:51:20.400 --> 01:51:23.000
including into their diet every day.

2257
01:51:23.000 --> 01:51:25.840
There's gotta be differences in absorption

2258
01:51:25.840 --> 01:51:29.390
as well, whey versus these plant alternatives.

2259
01:51:29.390 --> 01:51:32.400
And then amongst the different varieties

2260
01:51:32.400 --> 01:51:34.410
of plant proteins in terms of how well

2261
01:51:34.410 --> 01:51:37.650
the body can uptake these nutrients.

2262
01:51:37.650 --> 01:51:41.550
Yeah, you would be surprised when you isolate

2263
01:51:41.550 --> 01:51:44.370
the plant protein in any of these forms,

2264
01:51:44.370 --> 01:51:48.170
the absorption becomes almost comparable with whey,

2265
01:51:48.170 --> 01:51:51.600
and we're talking up into the 90% absorptions

2266
01:51:51.600 --> 01:51:53.450
in these isolated plant forms.

2267
01:51:53.450 --> 01:51:55.340
That's one of the big benefits of these.

2268
01:51:55.340 --> 01:51:58.340
They are very bioavailable and the difference

2269
01:51:58.340 --> 01:52:02.190
is probably only a couple of percent between them and whey.

2270
01:52:02.190 --> 01:52:05.670
And there are a bunch of randomized controlled trials

2271
01:52:05.670 --> 01:52:08.170
where they've compared whey with brown rice

2272
01:52:08.170 --> 01:52:10.470
and with pea, and looked at athletes

2273
01:52:10.470 --> 01:52:12.505
doing assistance training, and found no difference

2274
01:52:12.505 --> 01:52:16.590
between the two arms where one arm was supplementing

2275
01:52:16.590 --> 01:52:18.520
with whey, and one arm was supplementing

2276
01:52:18.520 --> 01:52:19.800
with the plant protein.

2277
01:52:19.800 --> 01:52:24.800
So I wouldn't be concerned about the bioavailability of them

2278
01:52:24.950 --> 01:52:29.950
and the protein researchers that are not,

2279
01:52:30.370 --> 01:52:33.180
they're not plant-based, these guys are omnivorous.

2280
01:52:33.180 --> 01:52:36.420
They all tend to agree now that as long

2281
01:52:36.420 --> 01:52:40.610
as the protein serve is right, it's ticking the box,

2282
01:52:40.610 --> 01:52:43.660
and lutein is at two or three grams,

2283
01:52:43.660 --> 01:52:45.690
then there is no difference between the two.

2284
01:52:45.690 --> 01:52:49.940
That's a huge shift from not that long ago

2285
01:52:51.090 --> 01:52:55.120
in terms of, what the scientific community is saying.

2286
01:52:55.120 --> 01:52:57.930
Yeah, there were some ideas that you would need

2287
01:52:57.930 --> 01:53:02.930
to consume much more plant protein to get the same effect.

2288
01:53:03.590 --> 01:53:08.590
And that's largely now been debunked

2289
01:53:08.690 --> 01:53:11.500
by two or three different studies.

2290
01:53:11.500 --> 01:53:14.850
As I say, that have looked at these isolated forms,

2291
01:53:14.850 --> 01:53:18.040
as long as the leucine is matched.

2292
01:53:18.040 --> 01:53:21.560
I will say that that seems to be why whey protein

2293
01:53:21.560 --> 01:53:25.690
in particular is good, is that it's high in leucine, right?

2294
01:53:25.690 --> 01:53:28.870
So as long as that plant-based protein powder

2295
01:53:28.870 --> 01:53:31.960
is meeting that two to three gram threshold,

2296
01:53:31.960 --> 01:53:33.403
then you can be comfortable

2297
01:53:33.403 --> 01:53:36.530
you are not sacrificing anything.

2298
01:53:36.530 --> 01:53:39.690
One question I've always had is given

2299
01:53:39.690 --> 01:53:43.030
that what we're trying to do is ensure

2300
01:53:43.030 --> 01:53:45.680
that we're getting those nine essential amino acids,

2301
01:53:45.680 --> 01:53:50.350
and when we eat foods, we break down those proteins

2302
01:53:50.350 --> 01:53:53.480
into their respective amino acid components,

2303
01:53:53.480 --> 01:53:56.410
instead of a protein powder supplement,

2304
01:53:56.410 --> 01:53:59.340
why not take a supplement of aminos

2305
01:53:59.340 --> 01:54:01.750
or branch chain amino acids,

2306
01:54:01.750 --> 01:54:05.540
so that you're bypassing that step of breaking them down

2307
01:54:05.540 --> 01:54:10.540
and creating perhaps an even more absorbable form of

2308
01:54:10.700 --> 01:54:12.400
the building blocks of protein?

2309
01:54:12.400 --> 01:54:15.630
Like, is that an ignorant statement, or how does that work?

2310
01:54:15.630 --> 01:54:20.630
It makes logical sense, but remember, these proteins

2311
01:54:20.750 --> 01:54:23.680
also contain non-essential amino acids,

2312
01:54:23.680 --> 01:54:26.490
and non-essential amino acids are important

2313
01:54:26.490 --> 01:54:28.470
for muscle protein synthesis.

2314
01:54:28.470 --> 01:54:31.400
And so your body is making those,

2315
01:54:31.400 --> 01:54:34.810
but when you're wanting to build a lot of lean muscle,

2316
01:54:34.810 --> 01:54:37.120
having more of those is helpful.

2317
01:54:37.120 --> 01:54:42.120
So if you were just taking the BCAA supplement

2318
01:54:42.490 --> 01:54:45.210
or an essential amino acid supplement,

2319
01:54:45.210 --> 01:54:47.410
you're missing out on all of those non-essentials.

2320
01:54:47.410 --> 01:54:51.830
So that's probably the first point that I would make there.

2321
01:54:51.830 --> 01:54:56.830
And I think largely particularly the BCAAs,

2322
01:54:58.020 --> 01:55:02.083
right, is when you are just taking the BCAAs,

2323
01:55:03.704 --> 01:55:06.980
you're not getting any benefit at all over

2324
01:55:06.980 --> 01:55:09.580
and above protein powder.

2325
01:55:09.580 --> 01:55:14.580
So my advice to people is that you could add the BCAAs,

2326
01:55:16.420 --> 01:55:19.510
but for the same price, you could add a good protein powder,

2327
01:55:19.510 --> 01:55:22.040
which is providing all of those other non-essential

2328
01:55:22.040 --> 01:55:25.290
and essential amino acids that are still critical

2329
01:55:25.290 --> 01:55:26.630
for building muscle.

2330
01:55:26.630 --> 01:55:29.510
It's not as though just leucine

2331
01:55:29.510 --> 01:55:32.480
and valine for example, which are often two

2332
01:55:32.480 --> 01:55:34.610
that people talk about, are the only ones

2333
01:55:34.610 --> 01:55:36.830
that matter, all of them matter.

2334
01:55:36.830 --> 01:55:40.040
And so providing your body with a good mix of all of them

2335
01:55:40.040 --> 01:55:42.990
is sort of generally the school of thought

2336
01:55:42.990 --> 01:55:44.690
and the recommendation for the best result.

2337
01:55:44.690 --> 01:55:46.510
Interesting, so don't waste your money on BCAA.

2338
01:55:46.510 --> 01:55:49.120
I wouldn't waste your money on BCAAs

2339
01:55:49.120 --> 01:55:51.440
or isolated amino acids.

2340
01:55:51.440 --> 01:55:53.960
I would stick to just finding a protein powder

2341
01:55:53.960 --> 01:55:57.630
that provides all of the nine-plus non-essential amino acids

2342
01:55:57.630 --> 01:55:58.900
in varying amounts,

2343
01:55:58.900 --> 01:56:02.793
and it's gonna be much more cost-effective too.

2344
01:56:03.680 --> 01:56:06.180
Conventional wisdom for a long time,

2345
01:56:06.180 --> 01:56:11.180
was that there's this special window post-workout,

2346
01:56:11.270 --> 01:56:15.090
about 30 minutes, in which you should replenish your body

2347
01:56:15.090 --> 01:56:18.650
with protein and other certain nutrients, electrolytes,

2348
01:56:18.650 --> 01:56:22.560
et cetera, to optimize the reparative cycle.

2349
01:56:22.560 --> 01:56:25.580
Is that still the case, has science pivoted

2350
01:56:25.580 --> 01:56:28.510
in terms of how we're thinking about that?

2351
01:56:28.510 --> 01:56:31.043
I think there's something in timing for sure,

2352
01:56:31.880 --> 01:56:34.340
and how much protein you're having at each meal.

2353
01:56:34.340 --> 01:56:37.840
But I think that if we were to sort of prioritize things

2354
01:56:37.840 --> 01:56:42.760
first it's, at first it's exercise and the stimulus,

2355
01:56:42.760 --> 01:56:44.207
and then it's your overall diet,

2356
01:56:44.207 --> 01:56:46.063
and then it's total protein.

2357
01:56:47.360 --> 01:56:51.090
And then underneath that, it's the timing of the meals,

2358
01:56:51.090 --> 01:56:52.930
and how much protein you're having in each meal.

2359
01:56:52.930 --> 01:56:56.550
So I don't want to kind of get carried away on this

2360
01:56:56.550 --> 01:56:58.550
because it's less important,

2361
01:56:58.550 --> 01:56:59.890
but if you're really fine-tuning,

2362
01:56:59.890 --> 01:57:02.240
this is where this stuff gets more important.

2363
01:57:02.240 --> 01:57:07.240
And the current evidence suggests that firstly,

2364
01:57:07.280 --> 01:57:09.790
instead of having, say you have 120 grams of protein

2365
01:57:09.790 --> 01:57:14.350
in a day, instead of having all of that in one meal,

2366
01:57:14.350 --> 01:57:17.090
from a muscle protein synthesis point-of-view,

2367
01:57:17.090 --> 01:57:19.620
and from a strength point-of-view, recovery point-of-view,

2368
01:57:19.620 --> 01:57:22.220
it seems that you are much better breaking that down

2369
01:57:22.220 --> 01:57:24.343
into three or four meals.

2370
01:57:25.420 --> 01:57:28.420
Breaking it down, not to the point where you have less

2371
01:57:28.420 --> 01:57:31.083
than 30 grams of protein in a meal,

2372
01:57:32.660 --> 01:57:36.100
but splitting it out over multiple meals throughout the day.

2373
01:57:36.100 --> 01:57:41.100
And the reason for this is that each time you have a meal,

2374
01:57:41.250 --> 01:57:46.250
you can spike muscle protein synthesis with, if your meal

2375
01:57:46.320 --> 01:57:50.350
is rich in protein and leucine, but it has a ceiling.

2376
01:57:50.350 --> 01:57:54.660
So if you have 120 grams at one point in the day,

2377
01:57:54.660 --> 01:57:57.400
you'll spike it, you'll hit that ceiling,

2378
01:57:57.400 --> 01:57:59.440
and then you get nothing else for the rest of the day.

2379
01:57:59.440 --> 01:58:00.273
Whereas when you--

2380
01:58:00.273 --> 01:58:02.710
So that additional protein gets metabolized

2381
01:58:02.710 --> 01:58:04.703
in some other way that doesn't lead to--

2382
01:58:04.703 --> 01:58:07.310
It's to be used for the body anabolic effect.

2383
01:58:07.310 --> 01:58:09.634
Yeah, but it's not gonna have the anabolic effect

2384
01:58:09.634 --> 01:58:14.420
and result in as much growth, muscle growth,

2385
01:58:14.420 --> 01:58:19.140
and strength improvement, compared to when you divvy it out

2386
01:58:19.140 --> 01:58:21.340
30 grams and then three hours later,

2387
01:58:21.340 --> 01:58:23.200
another meal with 30 grams of protein,

2388
01:58:23.200 --> 01:58:24.810
and then three hours later,

2389
01:58:24.810 --> 01:58:27.410
and then maybe it's three or four meals across the day.

2390
01:58:27.410 --> 01:58:32.020
You get multiple spikes of muscle protein synthesis,

2391
01:58:32.020 --> 01:58:35.370
and overall an a greater net effect

2392
01:58:35.370 --> 01:58:38.993
of muscle protein synthesis in that 24-hour period.

2393
01:58:40.100 --> 01:58:44.350
I want to get into intermittent fasting and all of that,

2394
01:58:44.350 --> 01:58:46.690
but I don't wanna go too deep into that right now.

2395
01:58:46.690 --> 01:58:48.530
I want to stick on what we're talking about,

2396
01:58:48.530 --> 01:58:51.210
but I do have a question that is perhaps pertinent,

2397
01:58:51.210 --> 01:58:56.210
which is there some kind of positive adaptation

2398
01:58:58.200 --> 01:59:01.333
that can be had for periodic,

2399
01:59:03.680 --> 01:59:06.440
a periodic sort of fasted workout,

2400
01:59:06.440 --> 01:59:09.640
fasted state, where let's say one day a week,

2401
01:59:09.640 --> 01:59:12.870
you do a hard workout and you don't eat

2402
01:59:12.870 --> 01:59:15.970
until many, many hours later,

2403
01:59:15.970 --> 01:59:17.800
you're kind of putting your body into

2404
01:59:17.800 --> 01:59:22.800
a stress situation that creates a certain adaptation.

2405
01:59:24.150 --> 01:59:26.200
That is something you don't wanna do every day,

2406
01:59:26.200 --> 01:59:30.600
but is there a benefit to experimenting with that?

2407
01:59:30.600 --> 01:59:35.350
I think it's plausible from a hormesis point-of-view

2408
01:59:35.350 --> 01:59:37.550
and David Sinclair talks about this,

2409
01:59:37.550 --> 01:59:40.600
and perhaps that's a way of activating

2410
01:59:40.600 --> 01:59:42.693
these disease resistance pathways,

2411
01:59:43.760 --> 01:59:47.090
but anyone who's involved in the protein research

2412
01:59:47.090 --> 01:59:49.443
and lean muscle will tell you not to do that,

2413
01:59:50.400 --> 01:59:52.360
because it's probably a good way to go

2414
01:59:52.360 --> 01:59:54.280
into a sort of catabolic state.

2415
01:59:54.280 --> 01:59:56.360
And if you're trying to preserve muscle

2416
01:59:56.360 --> 01:59:58.560
and you're an athlete, then I don't think

2417
01:59:58.560 --> 02:00:00.580
that's going to be the strategy you're going

2418
02:00:00.580 --> 02:00:02.570
to want to pursue.

2419
02:00:02.570 --> 02:00:06.090
You're better off consuming meals regularly

2420
02:00:06.090 --> 02:00:07.020
throughout the day.

2421
02:00:07.020 --> 02:00:09.440
Mm, it's interesting.

2422
02:00:09.440 --> 02:00:12.430
I mean, from an endurance athlete perspective

2423
02:00:12.430 --> 02:00:13.770
and not being a scientist.

2424
02:00:13.770 --> 02:00:16.070
Like I have played around with this

2425
02:00:16.070 --> 02:00:19.240
and I've had an experience where it's sort of like, okay,

2426
02:00:19.240 --> 02:00:23.180
my body knows that it can do this hard workout

2427
02:00:23.180 --> 02:00:25.570
and not be fed for a very long time.

2428
02:00:25.570 --> 02:00:28.520
So in the future, when I find myself

2429
02:00:28.520 --> 02:00:32.810
in a situation of semi-depletion,

2430
02:00:32.810 --> 02:00:34.797
I feel like I can push past that.

2431
02:00:34.797 --> 02:00:36.690
And maybe that's just a mental barrier

2432
02:00:36.690 --> 02:00:39.294
that an experience like that allows me

2433
02:00:39.294 --> 02:00:42.886
to believe that I can do a little bit more on less,

2434
02:00:42.886 --> 02:00:44.230
but I have to believe some sort

2435
02:00:44.230 --> 02:00:46.413
of biological component to that.

2436
02:00:46.413 --> 02:00:48.770
It would be an interesting study to do.

2437
02:00:48.770 --> 02:00:50.990
To take some endurance athletes and change,

2438
02:00:50.990 --> 02:00:52.900
adjust their meal timing throughout the day

2439
02:00:52.900 --> 02:00:55.490
and measure some meaningful biomarkers.

2440
02:00:55.490 --> 02:00:58.740
But yeah, it's certainly not out outta the question

2441
02:00:58.740 --> 02:01:02.020
that there is some adaptation and some benefit

2442
02:01:02.020 --> 02:01:02.853
to doing that.

2443
02:01:02.853 --> 02:01:07.800
Again, I think it comes back to what someone's goals are.

2444
02:01:07.800 --> 02:01:10.960
And I think if you were sort of erring on

2445
02:01:10.960 --> 02:01:14.420
the side of caution of preserving lean muscle mass,

2446
02:01:14.420 --> 02:01:17.640
definitely the research shows that you don't want

2447
02:01:17.640 --> 02:01:20.100
to be in a fasted state for too long.

2448
02:01:20.100 --> 02:01:24.723
You start catalyzing your own muscle tissue,

2449
02:01:25.590 --> 02:01:26.593
which is not good.

2450
02:01:28.420 --> 02:01:30.420
Unless you're trying to get super lean.

2451
02:01:30.420 --> 02:01:33.740
Yeah, and look, if you're trying to get super lean--

2452
02:01:33.740 --> 02:01:34.850
But that's not a very healthy way of doing it.

2453
02:01:34.850 --> 02:01:36.598
It's not that healthy.

2454
02:01:36.598 --> 02:01:41.540
And I mean, judging someone's health by the outside

2455
02:01:41.540 --> 02:01:43.340
is kind of fraught with danger.

2456
02:01:43.340 --> 02:01:44.930
Especially if you're looking at lean muscle,

2457
02:01:44.930 --> 02:01:46.650
we know this, you only have to look

2458
02:01:46.650 --> 02:01:51.650
at bodybuilders and their life expectancy is not amazing.

2459
02:01:51.800 --> 02:01:53.490
That could be many things going on there,

2460
02:01:53.490 --> 02:01:55.635
including anabolic steroids.

2461
02:01:55.635 --> 02:01:56.930
That might have something to do with it.

2462
02:01:56.930 --> 02:01:58.830
Yeah, but point being is

2463
02:01:58.830 --> 02:02:03.830
that it's this entire conversation

2464
02:02:04.620 --> 02:02:09.190
around preserving lean muscle mass and maximizing strength.

2465
02:02:09.190 --> 02:02:14.140
I do think at the core of it is a trade off.

2466
02:02:14.140 --> 02:02:17.140
I believe that's where the research points to,

2467
02:02:17.140 --> 02:02:20.790
the more we wanna squeeze out of growth

2468
02:02:20.790 --> 02:02:22.190
and increasing our strength,

2469
02:02:22.190 --> 02:02:26.180
I think we are potentially sacrificing longterm.

2470
02:02:26.180 --> 02:02:27.600
Yeah.

2471
02:02:27.600 --> 02:02:31.350
Back to the subject of supplements for athletes.

2472
02:02:31.350 --> 02:02:33.483
I mean, and just to say it out loud,

2473
02:02:35.280 --> 02:02:39.070
I'm not somebody who's taking a crazy number of supplements.

2474
02:02:39.070 --> 02:02:41.640
I believe in responsible supplementation,

2475
02:02:41.640 --> 02:02:44.960
but I always kind of err on the lesser side,

2476
02:02:44.960 --> 02:02:46.620
like there's very few things that I take

2477
02:02:46.620 --> 02:02:48.210
with any regularity, but this is

2478
02:02:48.210 --> 02:02:49.280
an interesting conversation.

2479
02:02:49.280 --> 02:02:53.210
So aside from protein powders,

2480
02:02:53.210 --> 02:02:54.610
what are some of the other things

2481
02:02:54.610 --> 02:02:57.090
that athletes might benefit from?

2482
02:02:57.090 --> 02:02:59.413
And particularly plant-based athletes.

2483
02:03:00.614 --> 02:03:03.710
So we talked about nitrates and L Citrulline,

2484
02:03:03.710 --> 02:03:08.280
the other, I guess, two that we could talk about are,

2485
02:03:08.280 --> 02:03:12.490
or three, there's beta-alanine.

2486
02:03:12.490 --> 02:03:14.480
I never hear about this.

2487
02:03:14.480 --> 02:03:17.530
So there's beta-alanine, creatine, and caffeine,

2488
02:03:17.530 --> 02:03:21.790
before I forget, those three, along with nitrate.

2489
02:03:21.790 --> 02:03:26.770
So consistently in all of the consensus position papers,

2490
02:03:26.770 --> 02:03:27.740
looking at the best science,

2491
02:03:27.740 --> 02:03:28.870
they're the ones that surface

2492
02:03:28.870 --> 02:03:32.280
as having the most ergogenic effect.

2493
02:03:32.280 --> 02:03:34.320
Well, let's start with beta-alanine.

2494
02:03:34.320 --> 02:03:37.660
Sure, so beta-alanine, alanine,

2495
02:03:37.660 --> 02:03:41.180
or alanine, is anyone who's taking this,

2496
02:03:41.180 --> 02:03:43.680
or some people that have taken this will have experienced

2497
02:03:43.680 --> 02:03:45.580
some paraesthesia.

2498
02:03:45.580 --> 02:03:50.580
You get, you can get tingles in your fingers.

2499
02:03:50.660 --> 02:03:53.560
Like, like when you overdose on niacin?

2500
02:03:53.560 --> 02:03:54.393
Yeah.

2501
02:03:54.393 --> 02:03:56.470
And there's a trick.

2502
02:03:56.470 --> 02:03:58.290
Remind me, I'll come back to that when talk

2503
02:03:58.290 --> 02:04:01.240
about dosage to try and avoid that.

2504
02:04:01.240 --> 02:04:04.690
But in short, what is beta-alanine doing?

2505
02:04:04.690 --> 02:04:05.995
It seems to be most effective,

2506
02:04:05.995 --> 02:04:09.400
short, bursive, high-intensive exercise.

2507
02:04:09.400 --> 02:04:11.790
We're talking up to 25, 30 minutes,

2508
02:04:11.790 --> 02:04:14.580
the research hasn't really gone beyond that.

2509
02:04:14.580 --> 02:04:16.230
And at a mechanism point-of-view,

2510
02:04:16.230 --> 02:04:20.310
beta-alanine increases carnosine,

2511
02:04:20.310 --> 02:04:24.850
and carnosine, essentially is like, it's an antioxidant.

2512
02:04:24.850 --> 02:04:27.360
You can think of it of the way I like to think

2513
02:04:27.360 --> 02:04:29.710
about carnosine is it's sort of mopping up all of

2514
02:04:29.710 --> 02:04:32.520
the free radicals we produce while we're exercising,

2515
02:04:32.520 --> 02:04:35.620
cleaning them out, and helps reduce fatigue.

2516
02:04:35.620 --> 02:04:38.793
So you can perform a higher power longer.

2517
02:04:40.640 --> 02:04:45.460
And we see quite significant improvements in power

2518
02:04:45.460 --> 02:04:48.670
and strength with be beta-alanine supplementation.

2519
02:04:48.670 --> 02:04:50.170
It's the typical dose.

2520
02:04:50.170 --> 02:04:53.420
And again, I'll put this into a document for you,

2521
02:04:53.420 --> 02:04:57.090
but high level it's about four to six,

2522
02:04:57.090 --> 02:05:01.580
this one is grams, four to six grams per day.

2523
02:05:01.580 --> 02:05:05.520
And the timing of this one is interesting.

2524
02:05:05.520 --> 02:05:07.380
For a long time it was thought that you have

2525
02:05:07.380 --> 02:05:09.655
to supplement this right before you work out.

2526
02:05:09.655 --> 02:05:13.870
That's kind of been disproven, and you can now spread

2527
02:05:13.870 --> 02:05:15.680
the supplementation out or take it whenever,

2528
02:05:15.680 --> 02:05:17.640
the most important thing is that you're just saturating

2529
02:05:17.640 --> 02:05:21.050
your cells with it, similar to what happens with creatine,

2530
02:05:21.050 --> 02:05:24.253
so that your baseline levels of carnosine go up.

2531
02:05:25.530 --> 02:05:27.900
So four to six grams,

2532
02:05:27.900 --> 02:05:31.060
and you could take that in one dose,

2533
02:05:31.060 --> 02:05:34.810
but that is where quite a lot of people get this tingling.

2534
02:05:34.810 --> 02:05:39.430
It's like a hot rash, itchy, it's uncomfortable.

2535
02:05:39.430 --> 02:05:43.200
And it's often put into those like hardcore pre-workouts,

2536
02:05:43.200 --> 02:05:45.890
that's the ingredient that's doing that.

2537
02:05:45.890 --> 02:05:47.923
So the strategy there--

2538
02:05:47.923 --> 02:05:50.030
Like the crazy stuff at GNC

2539
02:05:50.030 --> 02:05:53.160
that comes in like a bright red can

2540
02:05:53.160 --> 02:05:55.830
or can plastic tub or something.

2541
02:05:55.830 --> 02:05:58.370
Yeah, and they have a whole lot of things in there.

2542
02:05:58.370 --> 02:06:01.040
I am not a big advocate of those.

2543
02:06:01.040 --> 02:06:04.050
I think you're better off trying some of these targeted ones

2544
02:06:04.050 --> 02:06:06.440
where it's a single ingredient, or like two

2545
02:06:06.440 --> 02:06:08.680
or three ingredients, and seeing.

2546
02:06:08.680 --> 02:06:10.360
Does it come in like a capsule form?

2547
02:06:10.360 --> 02:06:12.220
You can get capsule or you can get a powder.

2548
02:06:12.220 --> 02:06:15.680
Usually it's a flavored, raspberry or lemon, or something.

2549
02:06:15.680 --> 02:06:20.210
And if you wanna avoid that paraesthesia,

2550
02:06:20.210 --> 02:06:23.210
because you don't have to take this as one single bolus

2551
02:06:23.210 --> 02:06:25.360
before you work out, you split it.

2552
02:06:25.360 --> 02:06:28.100
So it could be two or three serves throughout the day.

2553
02:06:28.100 --> 02:06:32.250
And then usually there's that removes that side effect.

2554
02:06:32.250 --> 02:06:33.940
So that's beta-alanine.

2555
02:06:33.940 --> 02:06:36.503
That's one for people to consider.

2556
02:06:37.630 --> 02:06:40.700
Creatine is the kind of obvious one.

2557
02:06:40.700 --> 02:06:43.670
Yeah, that's I mean, most people have heard of that.

2558
02:06:43.670 --> 02:06:48.393
It's sort of typical amongst the bodybuilding crowd.

2559
02:06:49.270 --> 02:06:50.690
What's interesting about creatine.

2560
02:06:50.690 --> 02:06:52.580
I mean, first of all, it's very effective.

2561
02:06:52.580 --> 02:06:55.410
So I want to understand better why that is.

2562
02:06:55.410 --> 02:06:58.970
But in recent years, very recently,

2563
02:06:58.970 --> 02:07:02.510
there seems to be coming out about the impact

2564
02:07:02.510 --> 02:07:04.890
of creatine on depression.

2565
02:07:04.890 --> 02:07:07.760
It's sort of this mood elevator and perhaps has

2566
02:07:07.760 --> 02:07:11.343
a positive impact on cognition, which is super interesting.

2567
02:07:12.230 --> 02:07:14.880
Yeah, the brain health side of things.

2568
02:07:14.880 --> 02:07:18.530
And it seems that it's, creatine is depleted often

2569
02:07:18.530 --> 02:07:21.093
in people with schizophrenia or depression.

2570
02:07:22.080 --> 02:07:25.103
So it does have a role beyond muscle.

2571
02:07:25.980 --> 02:07:28.440
And I think that's been underappreciated

2572
02:07:28.440 --> 02:07:30.840
certainly for a long time, and maybe we start on

2573
02:07:30.840 --> 02:07:34.323
the cognition piece and then we go into the performance.

2574
02:07:35.449 --> 02:07:40.449
There has been, it's very limited science looking

2575
02:07:41.170 --> 02:07:43.710
at creatine and brain health.

2576
02:07:43.710 --> 02:07:44.840
That's the first thing I wanna say.

2577
02:07:44.840 --> 02:07:47.333
It's very early days emerging.

2578
02:07:48.210 --> 02:07:50.680
At the moment, the current state of the literature is

2579
02:07:50.680 --> 02:07:54.030
that protocols have not yet been identified.

2580
02:07:54.030 --> 02:07:55.963
It's too preliminary for that,

2581
02:07:57.500 --> 02:07:59.000
they're, they've identified,

2582
02:07:59.000 --> 02:08:01.050
which is very interesting, that creatine,

2583
02:08:02.230 --> 02:08:04.720
our neurons actually produce creatine,

2584
02:08:04.720 --> 02:08:06.430
and the creatine in our brain is separate

2585
02:08:06.430 --> 02:08:08.850
to the creatine in the body for the most part.

2586
02:08:08.850 --> 02:08:13.170
So there is also a lot of question marks over

2587
02:08:13.170 --> 02:08:14.720
whether you just supplement orally

2588
02:08:14.720 --> 02:08:17.940
and does that increase the creatine levels in the brain?

2589
02:08:17.940 --> 02:08:19.620
Does it pass the blood brain barrier?

2590
02:08:19.620 --> 02:08:22.710
Yeah, and it may be that if you have depression

2591
02:08:22.710 --> 02:08:24.200
or you have a condition that affects

2592
02:08:24.200 --> 02:08:26.100
the blood brain barrier, it does cross,

2593
02:08:26.100 --> 02:08:28.530
or that it only crosses if you have depleted levels

2594
02:08:28.530 --> 02:08:29.363
in the brain.

2595
02:08:29.363 --> 02:08:34.363
And that is a very ongoing area of research.

2596
02:08:34.380 --> 02:08:36.170
So I think it's a watch the is space,

2597
02:08:36.170 --> 02:08:37.710
there could be some utility there,

2598
02:08:37.710 --> 02:08:39.060
there's something going on.

2599
02:08:40.520 --> 02:08:45.520
There have been talks of vegetarians in particular,

2600
02:08:46.340 --> 02:08:49.560
perhaps benefiting from creatine supplementation

2601
02:08:49.560 --> 02:08:51.670
from a cognitive point-of-view.

2602
02:08:51.670 --> 02:08:55.240
And the theory there is that, well, animal products

2603
02:08:55.240 --> 02:08:57.390
do contain a little bit of creatine.

2604
02:08:57.390 --> 02:09:00.360
Your body, it's not an essential compound.

2605
02:09:00.360 --> 02:09:04.240
Your body does make it, but there is some advantages,

2606
02:09:04.240 --> 02:09:05.560
at least from a performance point-of-view,

2607
02:09:05.560 --> 02:09:07.940
to have a bit more in your body

2608
02:09:07.940 --> 02:09:09.760
over and above what it makes,

2609
02:09:09.760 --> 02:09:13.290
and animal products do contain a little bit of creatine,

2610
02:09:13.290 --> 02:09:15.660
not enough to fully saturate the body with creatine,

2611
02:09:15.660 --> 02:09:18.480
unless you're gonna have two kilograms of meat or something.

2612
02:09:18.480 --> 02:09:20.450
But there has been this school of thought that

2613
02:09:20.450 --> 02:09:22.090
because there is some creatine coming

2614
02:09:22.090 --> 02:09:25.210
in through animal products,

2615
02:09:25.210 --> 02:09:27.720
perhaps vegetarians could benefit

2616
02:09:27.720 --> 02:09:29.420
from creatine supplementation

2617
02:09:29.420 --> 02:09:31.820
from a cognitive point-of-view.

2618
02:09:31.820 --> 02:09:36.330
And there's two studies that have come out

2619
02:09:36.330 --> 02:09:38.530
that I think are interest you to talk about here,

2620
02:09:38.530 --> 02:09:42.433
because I do think this is a little bit misunderstood.

2621
02:09:44.130 --> 02:09:46.980
The first is, and I think the most important is,

2622
02:09:46.980 --> 02:09:49.610
they have done neuroimaging and scanned

2623
02:09:49.610 --> 02:09:52.720
the brains of vegetarians and omnivores.

2624
02:09:52.720 --> 02:09:55.320
And they've been able to see that the creatine levels

2625
02:09:55.320 --> 02:09:57.958
in the brain are exactly the same, which is really,

2626
02:09:57.958 --> 02:09:59.790
really interesting.

2627
02:09:59.790 --> 02:10:03.360
And that probably is back to what I said earlier,

2628
02:10:03.360 --> 02:10:07.070
that our neurons are actually synthesizing creatine

2629
02:10:07.070 --> 02:10:08.680
separate to the rest of the body.

2630
02:10:08.680 --> 02:10:11.670
So that's different to what we see in muscles.

2631
02:10:11.670 --> 02:10:13.560
In muscle tissue, you see vegetarians

2632
02:10:13.560 --> 02:10:16.540
have less creatine than omnivores,

2633
02:10:16.540 --> 02:10:20.516
and which is one of main reasons why vegetarians potentially

2634
02:10:20.516 --> 02:10:23.580
have a better performance effect

2635
02:10:23.580 --> 02:10:25.253
from creatine supplementation.

2636
02:10:27.390 --> 02:10:30.990
There's a study that came out 2010

2637
02:10:30.990 --> 02:10:32.570
by a researcher called Benton,

2638
02:10:32.570 --> 02:10:35.400
and this is the kind of study that everyone cites,

2639
02:10:35.400 --> 02:10:39.300
looking at cognition between vegetarians

2640
02:10:39.300 --> 02:10:44.300
and omnivores with creatine supplementation.

2641
02:10:44.440 --> 02:10:47.210
So it was a randomized controlled trial, placebo.

2642
02:10:47.210 --> 02:10:52.210
And what they showed is there was a significant difference

2643
02:10:52.490 --> 02:10:57.360
in cognition between the vegetarians and the omnivores

2644
02:10:57.360 --> 02:10:59.390
that were supplementing with creatine.

2645
02:10:59.390 --> 02:11:02.440
But this study is misinterpreted.

2646
02:11:02.440 --> 02:11:04.110
So let me run through--

2647
02:11:04.110 --> 02:11:06.190
So this is the study that gets thrown around

2648
02:11:06.190 --> 02:11:09.110
on social media to establish that vegetarians

2649
02:11:09.110 --> 02:11:10.390
have some kind of brain problem?

2650
02:11:10.390 --> 02:11:12.787
Yeah, so let me just walk through exactly how,

2651
02:11:12.787 --> 02:11:14.350
how they did the study.

2652
02:11:14.350 --> 02:11:17.700
And we can just think about the findings here.

2653
02:11:17.700 --> 02:11:22.520
So baseline, they tested the cognition of the omnivores

2654
02:11:22.520 --> 02:11:23.580
and the vegetarians.

2655
02:11:23.580 --> 02:11:26.520
This was before supplementation, and this test,

2656
02:11:26.520 --> 02:11:28.240
this was a recall test.

2657
02:11:28.240 --> 02:11:32.940
So you're going to hear 30 different words.

2658
02:11:32.940 --> 02:11:35.550
And then you've got two minutes to write them down.

2659
02:11:35.550 --> 02:11:38.230
As many as you can, that was the cognitive domain.

2660
02:11:38.230 --> 02:11:39.433
It's a memory test.

2661
02:11:40.320 --> 02:11:44.640
At baseline, there was no difference between the two groups.

2662
02:11:44.640 --> 02:11:47.250
So the vegetarians and the omnivores

2663
02:11:47.250 --> 02:11:49.093
performed exactly the same.

2664
02:11:50.890 --> 02:11:53.960
Then they did creatine supplementation.

2665
02:11:53.960 --> 02:11:57.650
And this was a higher dosed creatine protocol

2666
02:11:57.650 --> 02:11:59.350
than what you would do for performance,

2667
02:11:59.350 --> 02:12:02.870
it was 20 grams a day over about a week period.

2668
02:12:02.870 --> 02:12:05.563
And they performed a test again.

2669
02:12:06.780 --> 02:12:08.603
And in that test,

2670
02:12:09.440 --> 02:12:14.380
the vegetarians performed as they did at baseline,

2671
02:12:14.380 --> 02:12:16.893
but the omnivores performed really poorly.

2672
02:12:17.790 --> 02:12:20.260
So there was a significant difference

2673
02:12:20.260 --> 02:12:23.050
between the two groups, but it wasn't driven

2674
02:12:23.050 --> 02:12:25.400
by the vegetarians performing poorly.

2675
02:12:25.400 --> 02:12:28.210
It was driven by the omnivores performing poorly.

2676
02:12:28.210 --> 02:12:32.373
So something about the creatine supplementation decreased

2677
02:12:33.430 --> 02:12:36.170
the omnivores' cognitive.

2678
02:12:36.170 --> 02:12:40.260
Perhaps, it was a very surprising finding.

2679
02:12:40.260 --> 02:12:43.240
And I think it's being misinterpreted.

2680
02:12:43.240 --> 02:12:48.240
As there's a vegetarians are deplete in creatine

2681
02:12:49.570 --> 02:12:52.150
and when you add it to their diet, their cognition improves.

2682
02:12:52.150 --> 02:12:53.230
That's not what the study showed.

2683
02:12:53.230 --> 02:12:56.690
Their baseline and their retest was exactly the same.

2684
02:12:56.690 --> 02:12:59.400
For some reason, the omnivores' performance

2685
02:12:59.400 --> 02:13:02.000
dropped off and that's what created

2686
02:13:02.000 --> 02:13:03.410
the significant difference.

2687
02:13:03.410 --> 02:13:08.410
So that's the Benton 2010 study, and Hamilton Roschel,

2688
02:13:09.150 --> 02:13:11.830
who's a big researcher in this space,

2689
02:13:11.830 --> 02:13:13.447
he just published a review called,

2690
02:13:13.447 --> 02:13:15.110
"Creatine and Brain Health."

2691
02:13:15.110 --> 02:13:18.460
It's fantastic for anyone to read about all of this.

2692
02:13:18.460 --> 02:13:21.160
And he essentially speaks about

2693
02:13:21.160 --> 02:13:23.690
the misinterpretations of that study,

2694
02:13:23.690 --> 02:13:25.160
talks about the fact that vegetarians

2695
02:13:25.160 --> 02:13:27.270
and omnivores have the same levels of creatine

2696
02:13:27.270 --> 02:13:31.890
in their brains on scans, and finishes by saying,

2697
02:13:31.890 --> 02:13:36.330
we need further research because for now we can't see

2698
02:13:36.330 --> 02:13:39.910
a significant reason for vegetarians to be supplementing

2699
02:13:39.910 --> 02:13:42.270
with creatine for brain health.

2700
02:13:42.270 --> 02:13:44.490
Hmm, that's fascinating.

2701
02:13:44.490 --> 02:13:46.890
So how does it get perverted and turned

2702
02:13:46.890 --> 02:13:49.650
into this narrative that gets thrown around

2703
02:13:49.650 --> 02:13:52.250
to kind of a line, you know?

2704
02:13:52.250 --> 02:13:54.290
I'm not sure it's intentional.

2705
02:13:54.290 --> 02:13:59.210
I think that if you'd sort of just look at one side of

2706
02:13:59.210 --> 02:14:01.935
the study and you've disregard the baseline,

2707
02:14:01.935 --> 02:14:04.890
and you just look at the two bars on this graph,

2708
02:14:04.890 --> 02:14:08.470
you see the vegetarians performing really well

2709
02:14:08.470 --> 02:14:10.030
compared to the omnivores.

2710
02:14:10.030 --> 02:14:14.410
So I think it's just a misinterpretation of the data

2711
02:14:14.410 --> 02:14:19.410
more than anything, but it, what it does say

2712
02:14:19.840 --> 02:14:22.050
is there's no reason to be alarmed

2713
02:14:22.050 --> 02:14:24.400
that if you're a vegetarian or a vegan

2714
02:14:24.400 --> 02:14:26.630
and you're not supplementing with creatine,

2715
02:14:26.630 --> 02:14:29.540
that you're going to have a cognitive deficit,

2716
02:14:29.540 --> 02:14:31.640
that science does not show that.

2717
02:14:31.640 --> 02:14:35.520
And while there will be more science done,

2718
02:14:35.520 --> 02:14:38.340
I think down the track, if they work out

2719
02:14:38.340 --> 02:14:42.880
a way to increase creatine levels in the brain

2720
02:14:42.880 --> 02:14:45.310
for certain conditions, whether it's schizophrenia

2721
02:14:45.310 --> 02:14:48.910
or depression, I think omnivores and vegetarians

2722
02:14:48.910 --> 02:14:52.110
will likely benefit in a similar manner.

2723
02:14:52.110 --> 02:14:55.100
Have they done studies on depression specifically?

2724
02:14:55.100 --> 02:14:57.030
Because you spoke about cognition,

2725
02:14:57.030 --> 02:15:00.240
but depression is an altogether different thing.

2726
02:15:00.240 --> 02:15:03.718
I haven't seen any of the data in terms

2727
02:15:03.718 --> 02:15:06.610
of supplementing people with depression

2728
02:15:06.610 --> 02:15:09.590
with creatine and seeing outcomes.

2729
02:15:09.590 --> 02:15:10.680
I can look into that.

2730
02:15:10.680 --> 02:15:14.860
But what I've seen is that people with depression

2731
02:15:14.860 --> 02:15:18.070
often have lower levels of creatine.

2732
02:15:18.070 --> 02:15:20.560
And I believe certainly the conclusion

2733
02:15:20.560 --> 02:15:23.360
of Hamilton Roschel's paper was

2734
02:15:23.360 --> 02:15:25.870
that we need far more information.

2735
02:15:25.870 --> 02:15:29.090
And even for conditions like depression and schizophrenia,

2736
02:15:29.090 --> 02:15:32.440
there is there's no science to date that gives us

2737
02:15:32.440 --> 02:15:36.860
very clear confidence to recommend a certain protocol

2738
02:15:36.860 --> 02:15:38.870
of supplementation for these people.

2739
02:15:38.870 --> 02:15:39.950
Got it.

2740
02:15:39.950 --> 02:15:44.700
So in the context of athletic performance,

2741
02:15:44.700 --> 02:15:48.550
there's some anabolic effect to creatine.

2742
02:15:48.550 --> 02:15:53.343
So walk me, help me and everybody understand what that is.

2743
02:15:54.450 --> 02:15:59.450
I guess, put simply, our body uses glucose

2744
02:15:59.680 --> 02:16:03.370
or carbohydrates into glucose that enters our cells.

2745
02:16:03.370 --> 02:16:05.970
People will have heard of the mitochondria,

2746
02:16:05.970 --> 02:16:08.210
and this is like the energy factory.

2747
02:16:08.210 --> 02:16:12.250
And through a whole sort of complex set

2748
02:16:12.250 --> 02:16:16.840
of biological reactions, we turn this glucose into ATP

2749
02:16:17.935 --> 02:16:21.200
and creatine allows you to produce more ATP.

2750
02:16:21.200 --> 02:16:23.100
And that is allowing you then,

2751
02:16:23.100 --> 02:16:28.100
to increase your power and your strength.

2752
02:16:29.460 --> 02:16:31.550
And the benefit of that is

2753
02:16:31.550 --> 02:16:34.420
that you can increase your training volume,

2754
02:16:34.420 --> 02:16:36.700
then therefore, get greater adaptations.

2755
02:16:36.700 --> 02:16:38.770
So it's not a situation

2756
02:16:38.770 --> 02:16:40.580
in which it just grows your muscle,

2757
02:16:40.580 --> 02:16:43.350
it just allows you to push harder, go longer?

2758
02:16:43.350 --> 02:16:46.520
And then as a result of that, gets stronger,

2759
02:16:46.520 --> 02:16:48.620
faster, et cetera.

2760
02:16:48.620 --> 02:16:51.490
For the most part, you will get a little bit of

2761
02:16:51.490 --> 02:16:53.840
a filling out with the water retention,

2762
02:16:53.840 --> 02:16:56.610
that can kind of make you feel a bit fuller.

2763
02:16:56.610 --> 02:16:58.580
Puffy.
Yeah, and some people

2764
02:16:58.580 --> 02:17:01.433
like that look, and others don't.

2765
02:17:02.300 --> 02:17:06.700
And I've definitely, the feedback I've had from,

2766
02:17:06.700 --> 02:17:09.450
in some endurance athletes is they don't like that.

2767
02:17:09.450 --> 02:17:12.100
And they think it works against their performance,

2768
02:17:12.100 --> 02:17:14.483
carrying that extra sort of water retention.

2769
02:17:16.140 --> 02:17:20.230
But by and large, it is just allowing you to do more work.

2770
02:17:20.230 --> 02:17:21.890
You get a greater stimulus

2771
02:17:21.890 --> 02:17:24.760
and then therefore greater adaptations.

2772
02:17:24.760 --> 02:17:29.350
And it's one of the safest, most studied ingredients,

2773
02:17:29.350 --> 02:17:34.350
safety up to 30, 30-plus grams per day with no side effects,

2774
02:17:37.110 --> 02:17:39.170
other than some gastrointestinal upset

2775
02:17:39.170 --> 02:17:40.360
in certain individuals.

2776
02:17:40.360 --> 02:17:43.490
So something to be aware of, but it's not that common,

2777
02:17:43.490 --> 02:17:45.730
certainly not as common as sodium bicarbonate,

2778
02:17:45.730 --> 02:17:48.330
which is another supplement that I really don't recommend

2779
02:17:48.330 --> 02:17:51.840
because it causes a lot of gastrointestinal upset,

2780
02:17:51.840 --> 02:17:53.540
even though it is quite ergogenic,

2781
02:17:54.820 --> 02:17:57.240
but creatine seems to not affect

2782
02:17:57.240 --> 02:18:00.390
that many people in that way.

2783
02:18:00.390 --> 02:18:04.090
And the dosing has, the recommendations have changed

2784
02:18:04.090 --> 02:18:06.300
over the years, used to be thought

2785
02:18:06.300 --> 02:18:09.330
you need to have a high dose, 20 grams a day,

2786
02:18:09.330 --> 02:18:13.150
for about a week, that will saturate your cells.

2787
02:18:13.150 --> 02:18:14.260
And then you can drop to

2788
02:18:14.260 --> 02:18:17.000
a maintenance dose of five grams per day.

2789
02:18:17.000 --> 02:18:18.570
That still is an option.

2790
02:18:18.570 --> 02:18:21.400
The, it's now also been shown that if you just jump straight

2791
02:18:21.400 --> 02:18:24.610
to five grams a day, by four weeks in,

2792
02:18:24.610 --> 02:18:26.180
you will have saturated your cells.

2793
02:18:26.180 --> 02:18:29.640
So you can choose your own adventure there.

2794
02:18:29.640 --> 02:18:30.473
Interesting.

2795
02:18:30.473 --> 02:18:32.980
I mean, I would think that much

2796
02:18:32.980 --> 02:18:36.650
like a bodybuilder has a bulk phase

2797
02:18:36.650 --> 02:18:38.980
and a lean phase, that an endurance athlete

2798
02:18:38.980 --> 02:18:43.180
could benefit from this by using it

2799
02:18:43.180 --> 02:18:45.810
during heavy training periods or training camps

2800
02:18:45.810 --> 02:18:49.990
to get the adaption, adaptation effects,

2801
02:18:49.990 --> 02:18:53.510
but then cycle off of it where they can lean out

2802
02:18:53.510 --> 02:18:56.170
and lose some of that water retention

2803
02:18:56.170 --> 02:19:00.278
that creates unnecessary, a weight drain,

2804
02:19:00.278 --> 02:19:02.073
where power to weight is so important

2805
02:19:02.073 --> 02:19:03.940
and that's in those sports.

2806
02:19:03.940 --> 02:19:05.600
Yeah, I think that makes sense.

2807
02:19:05.600 --> 02:19:08.840
And that's probably also what bodybuilders do

2808
02:19:08.840 --> 02:19:11.553
and when they're trying to lean out they jump off of it.

2809
02:19:11.553 --> 02:19:13.960
So, certainly there's nothing wrong

2810
02:19:13.960 --> 02:19:16.950
with using it like that in a sort of cycling,

2811
02:19:16.950 --> 02:19:18.350
cycle on, off fashion.

2812
02:19:18.350 --> 02:19:20.030
Right, and it does seem like it's safe.

2813
02:19:20.030 --> 02:19:22.690
I mean, is it, how do they manufacture it?

2814
02:19:22.690 --> 02:19:24.710
What is it comprised of?

2815
02:19:24.710 --> 02:19:25.630
That's a great question.

2816
02:19:25.630 --> 02:19:26.580
I always wonder,

2817
02:19:26.580 --> 02:19:30.000
I always assumed it wasn't a vegan product

2818
02:19:30.000 --> 02:19:32.260
because you associate creatine with--

2819
02:19:32.260 --> 02:19:36.820
Yeah, you certainly can get vegan creatine, 100%.

2820
02:19:36.820 --> 02:19:40.490
And the more and more now you're seeing brands

2821
02:19:40.490 --> 02:19:44.950
that are selling vegan creatine will have that on the label.

2822
02:19:44.950 --> 02:19:47.900
So I know that certain possible.

2823
02:19:47.900 --> 02:19:49.130
It's probably, it's synthetic,

2824
02:19:49.130 --> 02:19:51.740
so it's probably made in a laboratory.

2825
02:19:51.740 --> 02:19:54.000
Right, but relatively, basically

2826
02:19:54.000 --> 02:19:57.250
on the safer side of supplements that you're gonna take.

2827
02:19:57.250 --> 02:19:59.480
Definitely the, I mean, in all of

