3080
02:31:49.200 --> 02:31:50.860
there are a few reasons why I think they're good.

3081
02:31:50.860 --> 02:31:54.530
One is that I do think the calcium fortification

3082
02:31:54.530 --> 02:31:57.040
is important and we have to think

3083
02:31:57.040 --> 02:31:58.980
about someone's overall diet.

3084
02:31:58.980 --> 02:32:03.980
So if someone is looking to their milk

3085
02:32:04.230 --> 02:32:06.527
as a source of protein, and let's say it's providing

3086
02:32:06.527 --> 02:32:08.560
a very important source of protein

3087
02:32:08.560 --> 02:32:10.330
to that person's overall diet,

3088
02:32:10.330 --> 02:32:13.010
then when they make the swap to a plant-based milk,

3089
02:32:13.010 --> 02:32:16.140
they want to opt for one that is equivalent in protein.

3090
02:32:16.140 --> 02:32:19.260
And the obvious one is soy milk.

3091
02:32:19.260 --> 02:32:21.500
But now there are other alternatives

3092
02:32:21.500 --> 02:32:23.810
that are popping up, like pea milk, for example,

3093
02:32:23.810 --> 02:32:26.480
where both of those will have that sort of eight grams

3094
02:32:26.480 --> 02:32:31.120
of protein per serve, which is on par with the dairy milk.

3095
02:32:31.120 --> 02:32:34.880
So you have to know your overall dietary pattern

3096
02:32:34.880 --> 02:32:38.000
and what the purpose of adding this into your diet is.

3097
02:32:38.000 --> 02:32:41.750
If it's just being added to a coffee each day

3098
02:32:41.750 --> 02:32:45.310
in a very small amount, then that's a different conversation

3099
02:32:45.310 --> 02:32:48.100
because that person's going to want to look at it

3100
02:32:48.100 --> 02:32:51.203
more from a flavor and experience point-of-view.

3101
02:32:52.270 --> 02:32:56.710
But broadly speaking, I like to get people to look

3102
02:32:56.710 --> 02:33:00.030
for something that is as close to dairy milk

3103
02:33:00.030 --> 02:33:03.050
from a like, for like sort of perspective,

3104
02:33:03.050 --> 02:33:05.220
particularly if it's the main milk that they're going

3105
02:33:05.220 --> 02:33:08.550
to be drinking and have in their fridge for their family.

3106
02:33:08.550 --> 02:33:13.550
And so eight grams of protein and calcium fortification

3107
02:33:13.570 --> 02:33:18.570
at sort of that 100 milligrams per 150 mills.

3108
02:33:19.820 --> 02:33:21.890
So you can turn around and look per serve.

3109
02:33:21.890 --> 02:33:26.090
You should have around 300 milligrams of calcium

3110
02:33:26.090 --> 02:33:28.007
in a serve is exactly matched

3111
02:33:28.007 --> 02:33:31.010
for what you would get through dairy.

3112
02:33:31.010 --> 02:33:34.780
And then you're now starting to see, Rich,

3113
02:33:34.780 --> 02:33:37.680
some other plant-based milks pop up

3114
02:33:37.680 --> 02:33:42.680
that contain B12 and iodine, and vitamin D.

3115
02:33:43.460 --> 02:33:45.840
And again, whether you need these or not

3116
02:33:45.840 --> 02:33:49.490
really depends on back to our earlier conversation,

3117
02:33:49.490 --> 02:33:50.400
are you supplementing, are you getting enough--

3118
02:33:50.400 --> 02:33:53.360
Right, what does the rest of your diet look like?

3119
02:33:53.360 --> 02:33:54.550
On top of that,

3120
02:33:54.550 --> 02:33:56.350
you also have to learn how to read the labels.

3121
02:33:56.350 --> 02:33:58.740
Like a lot of these things have added sugar

3122
02:33:58.740 --> 02:34:00.770
and it's back to a conversation

3123
02:34:00.770 --> 02:34:03.050
around preservatives, emulsifiers,

3124
02:34:03.050 --> 02:34:06.000
all of these other things that go into creating

3125
02:34:06.000 --> 02:34:09.060
that texture that you're looking for in these products.

3126
02:34:09.060 --> 02:34:12.760
So some are more natural than others.

3127
02:34:12.760 --> 02:34:16.590
If it's, a lot of them have a lot, have added sugar.

3128
02:34:16.590 --> 02:34:19.170
I usually go for the unsweetened version.

3129
02:34:19.170 --> 02:34:22.850
That is, most brands will have, not all,

3130
02:34:22.850 --> 02:34:26.120
but a lot of them have a sweet version and an unsweetened.

3131
02:34:26.120 --> 02:34:29.410
Sure, and then there's the fat content as well.

3132
02:34:29.410 --> 02:34:31.410
Like a coconut milk is gonna be higher

3133
02:34:31.410 --> 02:34:34.130
in fat then the others, right?

3134
02:34:34.130 --> 02:34:37.270
Yeah, so if you are trying to limit your saturated fat,

3135
02:34:37.270 --> 02:34:39.130
then you're probably going to lean more

3136
02:34:39.130 --> 02:34:41.120
towards a pea milk or a soy milk.

3137
02:34:41.120 --> 02:34:43.560
And soy has particular properties actually,

3138
02:34:43.560 --> 02:34:45.530
that's very good for lowering cholesterol.

3139
02:34:45.530 --> 02:34:47.117
We can talk about that if you want at some.

3140
02:34:47.117 --> 02:34:49.610
People get freaked out when you talk about soy though.

3141
02:34:49.610 --> 02:34:51.950
Yeah, so that's why I like to state

3142
02:34:51.950 --> 02:34:54.150
and they don't need to get freaked out about soy,

3143
02:34:54.150 --> 02:34:55.750
but I understand that there is quite

3144
02:34:55.750 --> 02:34:57.333
a lot of stigma around it.

3145
02:34:58.200 --> 02:35:01.620
But the high quality science we have

3146
02:35:01.620 --> 02:35:04.410
suggests people don't need to fear it,

3147
02:35:04.410 --> 02:35:05.730
but for whatever reason,

3148
02:35:05.730 --> 02:35:07.830
some people don't want to consume soy.

3149
02:35:07.830 --> 02:35:09.530
And so I would look for other options,

3150
02:35:09.530 --> 02:35:13.720
like the pea milk that is comparable to dairy

3151
02:35:13.720 --> 02:35:16.860
in terms of overall protein content.

3152
02:35:16.860 --> 02:35:18.160
Oat milk seems should be killing

3153
02:35:18.160 --> 02:35:19.530
the game right now though.

3154
02:35:19.530 --> 02:35:20.790
Oat milk's great.

3155
02:35:20.790 --> 02:35:23.290
And it's, the reason it's going so well is

3156
02:35:23.290 --> 02:35:25.640
it's incredible in coffee.

3157
02:35:25.640 --> 02:35:27.390
It's very creamy.

3158
02:35:27.390 --> 02:35:31.230
My only sort of criticism,

3159
02:35:31.230 --> 02:35:32.760
if that's the right word, of oat milk,

3160
02:35:32.760 --> 02:35:35.430
is that if you are looking for something

3161
02:35:35.430 --> 02:35:38.790
that is comparable to dairy from a protein point-of-view,

3162
02:35:38.790 --> 02:35:41.690
if, for example, you want this to be one of

3163
02:35:41.690 --> 02:35:44.570
the sort of high-protein plant foods

3164
02:35:44.570 --> 02:35:46.240
that you are going to eat in the day,

3165
02:35:46.240 --> 02:35:48.640
then that's not the case for oat milk.

3166
02:35:48.640 --> 02:35:51.260
So just something to be aware of.

3167
02:35:51.260 --> 02:35:54.770
Mm, what about almond milk that you make at home

3168
02:35:54.770 --> 02:35:58.680
in three seconds in the Vitamix or cashew milk?

3169
02:35:58.680 --> 02:36:00.240
It's so easy.

3170
02:36:00.240 --> 02:36:02.320
Once you figure out how to do that.

3171
02:36:02.320 --> 02:36:06.320
It's easy, and my recommendation is if you do that,

3172
02:36:06.320 --> 02:36:08.580
then that's fantastic.

3173
02:36:08.580 --> 02:36:12.130
I would buy a red, you can buy red algae powder.

3174
02:36:12.130 --> 02:36:14.590
So back to the superfoods we were talking about,

3175
02:36:14.590 --> 02:36:18.270
and I would put red algae powder in, and red algae powder

3176
02:36:18.270 --> 02:36:20.180
is super constant traded in calcium.

3177
02:36:20.180 --> 02:36:21.380
You can't taste it.

3178
02:36:21.380 --> 02:36:24.640
And all of a sudden that transforms your milk

3179
02:36:24.640 --> 02:36:26.300
that you are making at home to one

3180
02:36:26.300 --> 02:36:27.450
that is packed with calcium.

3181
02:36:27.450 --> 02:36:29.727
Mm, that's a great hack, I never heard of that before.

3182
02:36:29.727 --> 02:36:31.430
And it's actually quite cheap.

3183
02:36:31.430 --> 02:36:33.120
And this one, I will name a brand

3184
02:36:33.120 --> 02:36:34.510
because I know it on the top of my head.

3185
02:36:34.510 --> 02:36:36.400
I think it's called NOW Foods

3186
02:36:36.400 --> 02:36:38.450
and they sell on Amazon around the world.

3187
02:36:39.350 --> 02:36:42.950
And they, at least they used to, when I last looked at this,

3188
02:36:42.950 --> 02:36:45.100
have a powdered form, not just a capsule.

3189
02:36:45.100 --> 02:36:49.478
So you can just dose that in at about,

3190
02:36:49.478 --> 02:36:52.830
you want to dose at about 1,000 milligrams of calcium

3191
02:36:52.830 --> 02:36:53.923
for one liter.

3192
02:36:55.010 --> 02:36:56.400
M'kay.

3193
02:36:56.400 --> 02:36:58.340
In the way that people get freaked out

3194
02:36:58.340 --> 02:37:00.620
when you talk about soy or soy milk,

3195
02:37:00.620 --> 02:37:05.000
people also get freaked out when the topic,

3196
02:37:05.000 --> 02:37:09.020
the subject turns to grains, right?

3197
02:37:09.020 --> 02:37:14.020
Whole grains are an important part of a healthy diet,

3198
02:37:14.390 --> 02:37:17.420
certainly a healthy whole food plant-based diet,

3199
02:37:17.420 --> 02:37:19.340
but then people lose their minds.

3200
02:37:19.340 --> 02:37:21.670
They're like, how can, grains are the devil,

3201
02:37:21.670 --> 02:37:23.250
grains are the worst thing that you could be eating?

3202
02:37:23.250 --> 02:37:26.743
How could you possibly say that I should be eating grains?

3203
02:37:28.490 --> 02:37:30.980
Yeah, so this comes back,

3204
02:37:30.980 --> 02:37:33.640
I think, the best sort of on-ramp here

3205
02:37:33.640 --> 02:37:35.840
or departure point to explain this is probably

3206
02:37:35.840 --> 02:37:38.560
that carbohydrates is an umbrella term.

3207
02:37:38.560 --> 02:37:42.460
And we often see all these different foods lumped

3208
02:37:42.460 --> 02:37:44.500
under the one sort of umbrella,

3209
02:37:44.500 --> 02:37:46.560
as well that's a carbohydrate-rich food,

3210
02:37:46.560 --> 02:37:48.340
it must be bad for our health.

3211
02:37:48.340 --> 02:37:53.210
And that stems from the most heavily processed cereal

3212
02:37:53.210 --> 02:37:55.390
to brown rice and quinoa,

3213
02:37:55.390 --> 02:37:57.000
and we see all these foods bucketed

3214
02:37:57.000 --> 02:38:00.240
underneath the same sort of umbrella.

3215
02:38:00.240 --> 02:38:03.840
And in reality, they have different effects on our health.

3216
02:38:03.840 --> 02:38:06.870
I think it's important to understand what's the difference

3217
02:38:06.870 --> 02:38:10.273
between a refined grain and an unrefined,

3218
02:38:11.120 --> 02:38:14.150
and takes me back to university.

3219
02:38:14.150 --> 02:38:17.410
I used to think the word beg.

3220
02:38:17.410 --> 02:38:22.410
So B stands for brand, E stands for endosperm,

3221
02:38:22.490 --> 02:38:25.550
and G stands for germ.

3222
02:38:25.550 --> 02:38:29.410
This describes the three layers of a whole grain,

3223
02:38:29.410 --> 02:38:32.060
and really the brand,

3224
02:38:32.060 --> 02:38:35.600
the outer layer is where most of the fiber is.

3225
02:38:35.600 --> 02:38:38.730
And then the endosperm in the middle is sort of

3226
02:38:38.730 --> 02:38:43.350
the largest component is just the starch carbohydrate part.

3227
02:38:43.350 --> 02:38:44.450
The white bread part.

3228
02:38:44.450 --> 02:38:47.330
Yes, and then the right deep, deep in,

3229
02:38:47.330 --> 02:38:52.330
there's the germ, and the germ is where

3230
02:38:53.030 --> 02:38:56.540
a lot of the antioxidants and phytochemicals, vitamins,

3231
02:38:56.540 --> 02:39:00.500
and minerals are, and in a refined grain,

3232
02:39:00.500 --> 02:39:03.440
you just have the endosperm, the middle layer.

3233
02:39:03.440 --> 02:39:05.130
So you just, you get rid of

3234
02:39:05.130 --> 02:39:08.850
the nice high-fiber outer casing,

3235
02:39:08.850 --> 02:39:12.330
and you get rid of this very nutrient-dense germ

3236
02:39:12.330 --> 02:39:15.170
from the middle, and you're just left with the starch.

3237
02:39:15.170 --> 02:39:18.430
Okay, so you can imagine, another analogy here is all of

3238
02:39:18.430 --> 02:39:23.120
a sudden, you've got your carbohydrates are naked,

3239
02:39:23.120 --> 02:39:25.060
they're not wearing their clothes anymore.

3240
02:39:25.060 --> 02:39:30.060
And whereas the whole grain is providing much more fiber,

3241
02:39:30.940 --> 02:39:33.470
much more antioxidants, phytochemicals,

3242
02:39:33.470 --> 02:39:34.963
vitamins, and minerals.

3243
02:39:35.810 --> 02:39:39.300
And they have very different effects on our physiology,

3244
02:39:39.300 --> 02:39:41.686
from how they're metabolized,

3245
02:39:41.686 --> 02:39:43.970
how they affect our gut microbiome.

3246
02:39:43.970 --> 02:39:46.200
If you're eating refined grains,

3247
02:39:46.200 --> 02:39:49.630
you're foregoing that fiber that you could have had,

3248
02:39:49.630 --> 02:39:52.400
and therefore, you're not feeding your microbes

3249
02:39:52.400 --> 02:39:53.920
at the same time.

3250
02:39:53.920 --> 02:39:58.150
So they are very different.

3251
02:39:58.150 --> 02:40:02.760
I like to point people to brown rice and wild rice,

3252
02:40:02.760 --> 02:40:05.380
and buckwheat and amaranth and barley.

3253
02:40:05.380 --> 02:40:09.340
These are all really, really healthy whole grains

3254
02:40:09.340 --> 02:40:11.600
that we should be including in our diet.

3255
02:40:11.600 --> 02:40:14.100
They are consistently associated

3256
02:40:14.100 --> 02:40:17.550
with better health outcomes, with longevity.

3257
02:40:17.550 --> 02:40:20.650
And usually I like people to be getting

3258
02:40:20.650 --> 02:40:24.340
at least three serves of those per day,

3259
02:40:24.340 --> 02:40:28.110
a serve being sort of half a cup of rice or quinoa,

3260
02:40:28.110 --> 02:40:31.343
or two pieces of whole wheat bread, for example.

3261
02:40:32.330 --> 02:40:37.330
And if you're doing that, you are absolutely

3262
02:40:38.020 --> 02:40:43.020
overall improving the overall healthfulness of your diet.

3263
02:40:43.420 --> 02:40:48.300
Okay, so for the consumer,

3264
02:40:48.300 --> 02:40:52.290
going to the market problems ensue,

3265
02:40:52.290 --> 02:40:54.220
because the there's a lot of confusion

3266
02:40:54.220 --> 02:40:56.420
about what constitutes a whole grain

3267
02:40:56.420 --> 02:40:57.540
versus a refined grain,

3268
02:40:57.540 --> 02:41:02.460
and there's a lot of marketing shenanigans

3269
02:41:02.460 --> 02:41:06.760
that go on into masking, what is a refined grain,

3270
02:41:06.760 --> 02:41:11.640
and trying to advertise it as something more

3271
02:41:11.640 --> 02:41:13.570
in the vein of a whole grain.

3272
02:41:13.570 --> 02:41:16.790
And so I think people are trying to make informed choices

3273
02:41:16.790 --> 02:41:18.650
and are often let astray.

3274
02:41:18.650 --> 02:41:21.410
So how do we know, like for example, bread,

3275
02:41:21.410 --> 02:41:23.540
like talk about bread a little bit,

3276
02:41:23.540 --> 02:41:25.090
because I think people would be amazed

3277
02:41:25.090 --> 02:41:26.490
to hear like, what goes into this?

3278
02:41:26.490 --> 02:41:27.990
Well, I used to just pick up

3279
02:41:27.990 --> 02:41:29.970
any sort of multi-grain bread.

3280
02:41:29.970 --> 02:41:32.420
Like if it's just on the darker side is probably better.

3281
02:41:32.420 --> 02:41:34.091
And if you can say some seeds.

3282
02:41:34.091 --> 02:41:36.640
I thought that was how you choose

3283
02:41:36.640 --> 02:41:39.330
a healthy bread, for a long time.

3284
02:41:39.330 --> 02:41:43.360
And it's probably not the best way of trying

3285
02:41:43.360 --> 02:41:46.910
to decipher what's healthy, what's less healthy.

3286
02:41:46.910 --> 02:41:50.118
And I like to point people to think

3287
02:41:50.118 --> 02:41:52.900
about two different things when trying to choose

3288
02:41:52.900 --> 02:41:54.900
a bread, but some of this applies

3289
02:41:54.900 --> 02:41:56.653
to just any food in a package.

3290
02:41:58.830 --> 02:42:02.120
The first is that the first ingredient written

3291
02:42:02.120 --> 02:42:05.430
on the bread on the ingredient list is very important,

3292
02:42:05.430 --> 02:42:06.560
very, very important.

3293
02:42:06.560 --> 02:42:07.940
Enriched flour.

3294
02:42:07.940 --> 02:42:09.420
If it's enriched flour,

3295
02:42:09.420 --> 02:42:11.760
then you know where all of a sudden we've jumped

3296
02:42:11.760 --> 02:42:14.240
into refined carbohydrate territory,

3297
02:42:14.240 --> 02:42:16.940
and that's probably going to be a product we want

3298
02:42:16.940 --> 02:42:19.220
to skip and look for something else.

3299
02:42:19.220 --> 02:42:21.580
Enriched is such an interesting choice of words.

3300
02:42:21.580 --> 02:42:25.346
It should be deprived flour or something like that.

3301
02:42:25.346 --> 02:42:27.080
I know it's a positive spin.

3302
02:42:27.080 --> 02:42:28.630
Impoverished, come on.

3303
02:42:30.846 --> 02:42:32.896
I don't blame them for using that word.

3304
02:42:34.100 --> 02:42:38.006
But the first word is very important.

3305
02:42:38.006 --> 02:42:41.980
We don't also, we also don't wanna see wheat flour,

3306
02:42:41.980 --> 02:42:44.180
wheat flour tricks a lot of people.

3307
02:42:44.180 --> 02:42:45.260
What you wanna see is

3308
02:42:45.260 --> 02:42:48.800
the first word is whole, whole wheat flour,

3309
02:42:48.800 --> 02:42:51.760
whole wheat grain, whole meal.

3310
02:42:51.760 --> 02:42:55.110
The very first part of that word should say whole.

3311
02:42:55.110 --> 02:42:56.500
Good luck finding that.

3312
02:42:56.500 --> 02:42:59.420
So there's almost no, you're, I mean, it's very difficult.

3313
02:42:59.420 --> 02:43:02.160
We're narrowing the field, but it's definitely,

3314
02:43:02.160 --> 02:43:04.730
it's definitely positive, definitely possible

3315
02:43:04.730 --> 02:43:05.883
to find one.

3316
02:43:07.230 --> 02:43:11.240
And the second thing I like people to look at,

3317
02:43:11.240 --> 02:43:12.430
which is really the final thing,

3318
02:43:12.430 --> 02:43:14.160
the two of these togethers works very well

3319
02:43:14.160 --> 02:43:16.200
to identify healthy bread,

3320
02:43:16.200 --> 02:43:21.200
is looking at the carbohydrate to fiber ratio.

3321
02:43:22.520 --> 02:43:27.520
So what we wanna see is a ratio of five to one or better.

3322
02:43:30.450 --> 02:43:34.300
So by that, what I mean is, if per serve

3323
02:43:34.300 --> 02:43:37.510
you have 20 grams of carbohydrates,

3324
02:43:37.510 --> 02:43:38.850
I wanna see that that product

3325
02:43:38.850 --> 02:43:42.520
has four grams of fiber or more.

3326
02:43:42.520 --> 02:43:45.010
That's a very good indicator, again,

3327
02:43:45.010 --> 02:43:47.360
that what we are dealing with here is

3328
02:43:47.360 --> 02:43:50.320
a less-refined product.

3329
02:43:50.320 --> 02:43:55.280
That goes for anything in a wrapper and also for breads.

3330
02:43:55.280 --> 02:43:57.520
That's interesting, I've never heard that before.

3331
02:43:57.520 --> 02:43:59.180
That's a good-- (crosstalk)

3332
02:43:59.180 --> 02:44:02.193
Attribute that, because, you who told me that?

3333
