that maybe would warrant a deeper look.

3391
02:46:38.190 --> 02:46:40.390
For sure, I think that's another good tip.

3392
02:46:41.760 --> 02:46:46.760
If your priority is lowering your cholesterol

3393
02:46:46.820 --> 02:46:50.890
or losing weight, like how do we, understanding

3394
02:46:50.890 --> 02:46:54.760
that there's no one-size-fits-all plant-based diet.

3395
02:46:54.760 --> 02:46:55.940
We talked about athletes,

3396
02:46:55.940 --> 02:46:58.090
we talked about some general principles.

3397
02:46:58.090 --> 02:47:01.450
How do you modify your approach to your plant-based diet

3398
02:47:01.450 --> 02:47:06.320
to achieve weight loss or lower those markers?

3399
02:47:06.320 --> 02:47:09.530
Usually when I talk about cholesterol lowering,

3400
02:47:09.530 --> 02:47:14.240
I point it to a series of recommendations

3401
02:47:14.240 --> 02:47:19.240
from an MD in Canada called Dr. David Jenkins.

3402
02:47:19.360 --> 02:47:24.360
And he has developed, what's called the Portfolio Diet.

3403
02:47:24.720 --> 02:47:26.410
Some people may have heard of this before.

3404
02:47:26.410 --> 02:47:29.370
It's a plant-based dietary pattern,

3405
02:47:29.370 --> 02:47:32.690
and it focuses more on what you are adding.

3406
02:47:32.690 --> 02:47:35.890
It's got four steps to it, and it's been clinically shown

3407
02:47:35.890 --> 02:47:39.320
in randomized controlled trials, to lower your cholesterol

3408
02:47:39.320 --> 02:47:41.836
by 30-odd percent.

3409
02:47:41.836 --> 02:47:45.020
And really that's not going full plant,

3410
02:47:45.020 --> 02:47:46.690
that's coming from an omnivorous diet.

3411
02:47:46.690 --> 02:47:49.620
So if you were to go full plant

3412
02:47:49.620 --> 02:47:52.330
and tap into these four recommendations even more,

3413
02:47:52.330 --> 02:47:56.450
then the cholesterol lowering could arguably be above 30%.

3414
02:47:56.450 --> 02:47:57.520
And I've certainly seen that

3415
02:47:57.520 --> 02:47:59.400
with the number of people I've worked with.

3416
02:47:59.400 --> 02:48:03.480
So the first recommendation of the four

3417
02:48:03.480 --> 02:48:06.397
in the Portfolio Diet, and I'll give you a PDF,

3418
02:48:06.397 --> 02:48:09.040
I have a beautiful PDF summary of this,

3419
02:48:09.040 --> 02:48:11.070
from Dr. David Jenkins.

3420
02:48:11.070 --> 02:48:16.070
First step is a couple of small handfuls of nuts per day.

3421
02:48:17.550 --> 02:48:21.450
So that could be walnuts, could be pistachios,

3422
02:48:21.450 --> 02:48:22.290
could be almonds.

3423
02:48:22.290 --> 02:48:25.260
It could be a serve of nut butter,

3424
02:48:25.260 --> 02:48:27.000
which is a tablespoon or two.

3425
02:48:27.000 --> 02:48:30.150
It's interesting, I wouldn't intuitively associate those

3426
02:48:30.150 --> 02:48:31.980
with lowering cholesterol.

3427
02:48:31.980 --> 02:48:35.470
So let me tell you what's happening there.

3428
02:48:35.470 --> 02:48:37.250
Nuts consistently have been shown

3429
02:48:37.250 --> 02:48:39.440
in the literature to lower cholesterol.

3430
02:48:39.440 --> 02:48:43.090
And the reason for that is their unsaturated fat content,

3431
02:48:43.090 --> 02:48:45.313
particularly the polyunsaturated fats,

3432
02:48:46.640 --> 02:48:49.340
which, as opposed to saturated fat

3433
02:48:49.340 --> 02:48:52.260
which increases cholesterol, unsaturated fats,

3434
02:48:52.260 --> 02:48:54.450
particularly at the poly unsaturated fats,

3435
02:48:54.450 --> 02:48:56.130
lower cholesterol.

3436
02:48:56.130 --> 02:48:58.670
So that's what's happening there.

3437
02:48:58.670 --> 02:49:03.670
The second recommendation in the Portfolio Diet is to have

3438
02:49:05.300 --> 02:49:10.053
at least two to three serves of plant protein per day,

3439
02:49:11.090 --> 02:49:14.680
ideally with a few of those being from soy foods.

3440
02:49:14.680 --> 02:49:18.920
So this overall, could be two or three serves from lentils,

3441
02:49:18.920 --> 02:49:22.800
chickpeas, tofu, tempeh, these sorts of foods.

3442
02:49:22.800 --> 02:49:26.270
The reason for a recommendation to include some soy foods

3443
02:49:26.270 --> 02:49:30.020
within that, edamame, for example, or tofu,

3444
02:49:30.020 --> 02:49:35.020
is that they do have a particularly good way

3445
02:49:35.180 --> 02:49:38.080
of lowering cholesterol, and--

3446
02:49:38.080 --> 02:49:39.510
That's unique to soy.

3447
02:49:39.510 --> 02:49:42.800
That's unique to soy and it's probably driven

3448
02:49:42.800 --> 02:49:45.303
actually through polyphenols,

3449
02:49:46.270 --> 02:49:48.080
the phytoestrogens, which is the,

3450
02:49:48.080 --> 02:49:50.450
what everyone sort of refers to them as,

3451
02:49:50.450 --> 02:49:54.020
they're actually isoflavones, which are polyphenols.

3452
02:49:54.020 --> 02:49:58.060
And it does seem that about one in two people

3453
02:49:58.060 --> 02:50:01.340
have a particular microbiome composition

3454
02:50:01.340 --> 02:50:04.090
where they can convert these compounds

3455
02:50:04.090 --> 02:50:06.930
into a compound called equol,

3456
02:50:06.930 --> 02:50:10.150
which is providing many benefits throughout the body.

3457
02:50:10.150 --> 02:50:13.580
So two to three serves

3458
02:50:13.580 --> 02:50:16.310
of plant protein being tip number two.

3459
02:50:16.310 --> 02:50:19.190
And remember that this is for most people,

3460
02:50:19.190 --> 02:50:23.533
coming at the expense of red meat and chicken.

3461
02:50:24.910 --> 02:50:29.910
The third recommendation is to have five serves

3462
02:50:30.620 --> 02:50:33.750
of fruits and vegetables per day,

3463
02:50:33.750 --> 02:50:36.510
five serves of fruits and vegetables per day,

3464
02:50:36.510 --> 02:50:40.330
which is well above what the average intake is.

3465
02:50:40.330 --> 02:50:44.500
And with a bias towards fruits and vegetables

3466
02:50:44.500 --> 02:50:48.640
that have a lot of soluble fiber, viscous fiber,

3467
02:50:48.640 --> 02:50:52.090
that pulls bile out of the digestive system,

3468
02:50:52.090 --> 02:50:54.403
and in doing that, helps to lower cholesterol.

3469
02:50:55.530 --> 02:50:59.613
These sort of viscous foods are like eggplant, okra.

3470
02:51:00.720 --> 02:51:04.910
We've got berries are another great one, apples,

3471
02:51:04.910 --> 02:51:07.740
so these sorts of foods.

3472
02:51:07.740 --> 02:51:10.650
And then the fourth tip is,

3473
02:51:10.650 --> 02:51:15.160
or fourth recommendation within this Portfolio Diet is

3474
02:51:15.160 --> 02:51:18.610
the consumption of plant sterols.

3475
02:51:18.610 --> 02:51:23.313
So these are a phytochemical that essentially blocks

3476
02:51:24.910 --> 02:51:27.770
the absorption of cholesterol.

3477
02:51:27.770 --> 02:51:30.420
And you can do this.

3478
02:51:30.420 --> 02:51:32.290
There are some products that are fortified

3479
02:51:32.290 --> 02:51:36.690
with these plant sterols, but probably the best

3480
02:51:37.540 --> 02:51:40.800
and easiest way to do this, because you need two grams

3481
02:51:40.800 --> 02:51:44.420
of these plant sterols per day to be clinically effective,

3482
02:51:44.420 --> 02:51:48.350
that's shown in randomized controlled trials,

3483
02:51:48.350 --> 02:51:50.370
is to take a supplement.

3484
02:51:50.370 --> 02:51:53.070
And there's a bunch of different brands offering them,

3485
02:51:53.070 --> 02:51:55.380
and they're pretty much always at two grams per serve

3486
02:51:55.380 --> 02:51:58.083
because that is the clinically proven dose.

3487
02:51:59.120 --> 02:52:02.990
So those are the four sort of recommendations that

3488
02:52:04.360 --> 02:52:07.200
on the aggregate, lead to a 30% reduction

3489
02:52:07.200 --> 02:52:09.310
in your LDL cholesterol,

3490
02:52:09.310 --> 02:52:10.990
which is the atherogenic cholesterol

3491
02:52:10.990 --> 02:52:13.628
that contributes to the fatty plaque being laid down

3492
02:52:13.628 --> 02:52:17.140
in our arteries, and then in a heart attack or a stroke.

3493
02:52:17.140 --> 02:52:21.450
I would say, because that can be quite a significant drop,

3494
02:52:21.450 --> 02:52:25.820
if you are currently on medications,

3495
02:52:25.820 --> 02:52:28.440
you should be doing this under

3496
02:52:28.440 --> 02:52:30.210
the supervision of your physician.

3497
02:52:30.210 --> 02:52:33.040
You should at least let them know that, look,

3498
02:52:33.040 --> 02:52:34.582
I'm gonna be changing my diet.

3499
02:52:34.582 --> 02:52:39.080
And you could point to this PDF that I will provide.

3500
02:52:39.080 --> 02:52:41.640
At which point the doctor says, go for it.

3501
02:52:41.640 --> 02:52:43.070
It's not gonna make any difference.

3502
02:52:43.070 --> 02:52:45.490
Your statin is always gonna be your statin.

3503
02:52:45.490 --> 02:52:48.940
Right, and you might be the first person

3504
02:52:48.940 --> 02:52:50.750
that goes back and surprises them.

3505
02:52:50.750 --> 02:52:53.170
But the point of keeping them across it is

3506
02:52:53.170 --> 02:52:56.910
that it may well affect your dose of your medication.

3507
02:52:56.910 --> 02:52:57.743
Right.

3508
02:52:59.420 --> 02:53:02.403
It seems like these are well, two things, first,

3509
02:53:03.700 --> 02:53:07.550
by eating these foods, you kind of crowding out

3510
02:53:07.550 --> 02:53:10.510
the other foods that might take up space on your plate.

3511
02:53:10.510 --> 02:53:13.300
So it's not about what you're eliminating,

3512
02:53:13.300 --> 02:53:15.210
it's about focusing on these new things.

3513
02:53:15.210 --> 02:53:16.810
And then suddenly, there's no room

3514
02:53:16.810 --> 02:53:17.760
for all those other things

3515
02:53:17.760 --> 02:53:20.060
that are elevating your cholesterol.

3516
02:53:20.060 --> 02:53:23.020
But beyond that, with the exception of maybe amping

3517
02:53:23.020 --> 02:53:26.540
up your fruit and vegetable intake,

3518
02:53:26.540 --> 02:53:29.530
these seem like principles that are good for anybody,

3519
02:53:29.530 --> 02:53:31.590
whether you're trying to lower your cholesterol or not.

3520
02:53:31.590 --> 02:53:32.720
100%, yeah.

3521
02:53:32.720 --> 02:53:36.990
And, overall, it's just shifting people

3522
02:53:36.990 --> 02:53:40.746
to a whole food plant-based dietary pattern.

3523
02:53:40.746 --> 02:53:45.530
It's just that it has, that specific protocol

3524
02:53:45.530 --> 02:53:48.540
has been tried and tested, and has shown

3525
02:53:48.540 --> 02:53:52.240
to result in this very clinically meaningful drop

3526
02:53:52.240 --> 02:53:56.090
in cholesterol, which is equivalent to low dose statins.

3527
02:53:56.090 --> 02:54:01.090
So that 30% reduction is very significant.

3528
02:54:01.710 --> 02:54:04.840
For the average person that's taking their cholesterol

3529
02:54:04.840 --> 02:54:08.883
from 130, which as we established is well above optimal,

3530
02:54:09.980 --> 02:54:14.270
down to 90 or around 90, which is a moving

3531
02:54:14.270 --> 02:54:16.530
in a very favorable direction.

3532
02:54:16.530 --> 02:54:19.000
And this is something that has been proven out.

3533
02:54:19.000 --> 02:54:22.570
Plenty of people have done this effectively.

3534
02:54:22.570 --> 02:54:23.403
Lower their--

3535
02:54:23.403 --> 02:54:27.150
Many different studies tried and tested.

3536
02:54:27.150 --> 02:54:29.260
And in fact, it's so tried and tested

3537
02:54:29.260 --> 02:54:32.790
that most physicians, if presented with this,

3538
02:54:32.790 --> 02:54:34.360
will be well aware of it.

3539
02:54:34.360 --> 02:54:37.970
It's a very commonly understood protocol

3540
02:54:37.970 --> 02:54:40.810
and has now influenced some of

3541
02:54:40.810 --> 02:54:44.030
the national cholesterol-lowering dietary guidelines.

3542
02:54:44.030 --> 02:54:45.570
Oh, that's good to hear.

3543
02:54:45.570 --> 02:54:49.170
How would this differ if weight loss is the priority,

3544
02:54:49.170 --> 02:54:52.240
beyond the obvious, like maybe reduce your portions.

3545
02:54:52.240 --> 02:54:55.270
Like, what are the kind of tweaks that you're gonna make,

3546
02:54:55.270 --> 02:54:56.533
if that's your goal?

3547
02:54:58.610 --> 02:55:02.623
Firstly, understanding calorie density is important.

3548
02:55:03.640 --> 02:55:06.580
In my book, I separate foods

3549
02:55:06.580 --> 02:55:08.560
into sort of low calorie density,

3550
02:55:08.560 --> 02:55:12.340
medium calorie density, high calorie density, and very high.

3551
02:55:12.340 --> 02:55:15.620
And the low calorie-dense foods are pretty

3552
02:55:15.620 --> 02:55:18.260
much all of your fruits and vegetables,

3553
02:55:18.260 --> 02:55:20.490
other than say dates and avocados,

3554
02:55:20.490 --> 02:55:21.600
which are very healthy foods,

3555
02:55:21.600 --> 02:55:24.480
but are just a bit more calorie-dense.

3556
02:55:24.480 --> 02:55:28.570
So in that low-calorie sort of food table,

3557
02:55:28.570 --> 02:55:30.280
I have all the fruits and vegetables.

3558
02:55:30.280 --> 02:55:31.770
It's got the dark leafy greens.

3559
02:55:31.770 --> 02:55:33.270
It's got the cruciferous vegetables,

3560
02:55:33.270 --> 02:55:35.890
like broccoli and cabbage, and broccolini.

3561
02:55:36.760 --> 02:55:41.330
It's got pretty much all of your various fruits.

3562
02:55:41.330 --> 02:55:44.150
It's got mushrooms, and it also has tofu in there.

3563
02:55:44.150 --> 02:55:47.140
And usually if someone comes to me and they're wanting

3564
02:55:47.140 --> 02:55:51.440
to lose weight, let's say that's their goal,

3565
02:55:51.440 --> 02:55:53.220
that's right for them.

3566
02:55:53.220 --> 02:55:56.300
First, I check, are they eating according

3567
02:55:56.300 --> 02:55:58.680
to sort of the plant-based food pyramid

3568
02:55:58.680 --> 02:56:00.200
that I have in there, or has a whole lot

3569
02:56:00.200 --> 02:56:02.380
of ultra processed foods snuck in,

3570
02:56:02.380 --> 02:56:03.773
which sometimes can happen.

3571
02:56:04.609 --> 02:56:07.790
In which case you just remove those and you barely have

3572
02:56:07.790 --> 02:56:10.340
to worry about anything else, and it takes care of itself.

3573
02:56:10.340 --> 02:56:12.569
Right, those are hyperpalatable

3574
02:56:12.569 --> 02:56:14.800
and they're driving that excess consumption.

3575
02:56:14.800 --> 02:56:17.780
And we can't control the environment around us,

3576
02:56:17.780 --> 02:56:19.800
but we can try as best as possible to control

3577
02:56:19.800 --> 02:56:21.620
the environment in our four walls.

3578
02:56:21.620 --> 02:56:23.070
And at least make it harder,

3579
02:56:23.070 --> 02:56:26.740
and create more resistance to consuming those foods.

3580
02:56:26.740 --> 02:56:28.280
So if they're not in the house,

3581
02:56:28.280 --> 02:56:29.973
if the ice cream's not there,

3582
02:56:31.020 --> 02:56:32.610
you have to overcome a lot of resistance

3583
02:56:32.610 --> 02:56:34.910
to jump into the car when you get the craving.

3584
02:56:36.520 --> 02:56:37.870
Calorie density,

3585
02:56:37.870 --> 02:56:40.470
back to those four different sort of groups,

3586
02:56:40.470 --> 02:56:44.350
are plant-based foods, whole foods, whole plant-based foods.

3587
02:56:44.350 --> 02:56:48.437
My recommendation is to really load up on those fruits

3588
02:56:48.437 --> 02:56:51.610
and vegetables, particularly before your main meal is

3589
02:56:51.610 --> 02:56:56.610
a way of filling up, and it will improve your satiety

3590
02:56:58.050 --> 02:57:00.260
before you get more of the calorie-dense foods

3591
02:57:00.260 --> 02:57:01.540
on your plate.

3592
02:57:01.540 --> 02:57:05.300
And one of the sort of superstars

3593
02:57:05.300 --> 02:57:08.663
that often people are surprised by here, is potato.

3594
02:57:09.840 --> 02:57:12.870
It's, potato is a much malaligned food,

3595
02:57:12.870 --> 02:57:16.950
largely because we fry it and turn it into chips.

3596
02:57:16.950 --> 02:57:21.790
But if you just take the sort of boiled or baked potato

3597
02:57:21.790 --> 02:57:25.630
and look at that, it is a very satiating food.

3598
02:57:25.630 --> 02:57:27.830
It's low in calories.

3599
02:57:27.830 --> 02:57:32.310
So it's a great way to feel full on fewer calories.

3600
02:57:32.310 --> 02:57:34.460
And it actually has a lot more nutrients

3601
02:57:34.460 --> 02:57:37.360
than people realize, like even the average russet potato

3602
02:57:37.360 --> 02:57:39.210
is pretty good.

3603
02:57:39.210 --> 02:57:43.160
If you just don't put a ton of butter on it, or sour cream

3604
02:57:43.160 --> 02:57:46.660
or whatever, and just eat it for what it is, it's filling.

3605
02:57:46.660 --> 02:57:49.810
This is something Chef AJ talks a lot about, like,

3606
02:57:49.810 --> 02:57:53.913
if you just increase those low calorie density foods

3607
02:57:53.913 --> 02:57:57.810
that are super high in fiber, you can fill yourself up.

3608
02:57:57.810 --> 02:58:01.000
And I think kind of pre-loading before your meal

3609
02:58:01.000 --> 02:58:03.500
so that you don't go into a meal starving,

3610
02:58:03.500 --> 02:58:07.070
you're in a better place to make better selective decisions.

3611
02:58:07.070 --> 02:58:08.390
Definitely.
That's great advice.

3612
02:58:08.390 --> 02:58:11.020
Like big salads before you go into your main meal.

3613
02:58:11.020 --> 02:58:13.270
Cauliflower is another one in there.

3614
02:58:13.270 --> 02:58:16.740
And being aware of the hidden calorie bombs.

3615
02:58:16.740 --> 02:58:18.300
Like what dressing are you using?

3616
02:58:18.300 --> 02:58:20.210
What is the, it's all in the sauces

3617
02:58:20.210 --> 02:58:22.530
and all the other stuff that seems benign,

3618
02:58:22.530 --> 02:58:24.670
and those are the real killers.

3619
02:58:24.670 --> 02:58:25.960
And there, so there's a study

3620
02:58:25.960 --> 02:58:27.800
that speaks pretty much to that

3621
02:58:27.800 --> 02:58:30.650
out of John's Hopkins, that looked at

3622
02:58:30.650 --> 02:58:32.670
how many extra calories does someone consume

3623
02:58:32.670 --> 02:58:35.820
if they eat out like five, six times a week,

3624
02:58:35.820 --> 02:58:39.230
versus someone who cooks at home almost every day.

3625
02:58:39.230 --> 02:58:43.360
And they were able to determine that

3626
02:58:43.360 --> 02:58:46.170
that person eating out just five or six meals a week,

3627
02:58:46.170 --> 02:58:49.410
were eating on average 1,000 calories more per week,

3628
02:58:49.410 --> 02:58:52.130
which over the course of the year is equivalent

3629
02:58:52.130 --> 02:58:53.973
to around seven kilograms of butter.

3630
02:58:55.770 --> 02:58:58.630
So, and probably what's happening there is

3631
02:58:58.630 --> 02:59:01.500
that in restaurants and in cafes,

3632
02:59:01.500 --> 02:59:03.240
there are a lot of hidden calories in the--

3633
02:59:03.240 --> 02:59:05.320
Sure, they're just trying to make it taste good.

3634
02:59:05.320 --> 02:59:07.760
And they're not showing you a nutrition profile

3635
02:59:07.760 --> 02:59:10.340
on this food, and they're gonna slather it with stuff,

3636
02:59:10.340 --> 02:59:13.020
whether they tell you or not, for the most part.

3637
02:59:13.020 --> 02:59:17.050
The chefs call it SOS, salt, oil, and sugar.

3638
02:59:17.050 --> 02:59:18.044
And that's a--

3639
02:59:18.044 --> 02:59:19.503
That's what Alan Goldhammer calls--

3640
02:59:19.503 --> 02:59:22.090
It's a secret weapon for them

3641
02:59:22.090 --> 02:59:24.420
to make the food more appealing.

